window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-14"] = [{"id":1,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第一章：成績單大風暴\n\n星期三下午，鹿陽國小六年一班的教室裡，正在舉行一場比颱風警報還恐怖的發布會。\n\n講台上的高峙舷老師推了推黑框眼鏡，鏡片後的瞳孔閃過一道幽藍色的微光：\n\n「各位同學，根據教育局公告，六年級全國統一命題月考，將於下週三登場。考試範圍：國語第一至五課、數學第一至四單元、自然第一至三單元、社會……」\n\n「噹啷！」\n\n老巫嘴裡的肉包直接掉在桌上。他兩眼發直，聲音抖得像是冬天裡的落葉：\n\n「老、老師……我光是聽到『社會』兩個字，就覺得整個世界都不『社會』了……」\n\n阿釁趴在桌上，淒厲哀嚎：「完蛋了！月考！我媽說了，這次再吊車尾，就把我的遊戲機鎖進保險箱，讓我整個暑假跟補習班結拜！」\n\n這句話像點燃了導火線。全班二十六張臉，齊刷刷地拉成了苦瓜。\n\n「肅靜！」\n\n教室門口，一道低沉嚴厲的嗓音像冷氣一樣灌了進來，全班瞬間被按下靜音鍵。\n\n學務主任周嚴倒背著雙手，鷹隼般的目光掃過全班，手裡的違規登記簿已經翻到了最新一頁：\n\n「月考期間，本校將執行史上最嚴格考場規定！凡夾帶、傳紙條、打暗號，一律依校規記過處分！六年一班，你們這群皮蛋給我聽清楚了——不要讓我周嚴，在違規名單上看到你們的名字！」\n\n周主任前腳剛走，天花板通風管裡立刻「嗖」地探出一顆似鼠似狐的小腦袋。\n\n班級 AI 智慧小寵物溜溜甩了甩金屬光澤的大尾巴，電子眼狂閃紅光：\n\n「嗶嗶！黑面判官氣場指數：九十九！負能量覆蓋全走廊！建議全班撤退至安全距離五十公尺以上！」\n\n「撤你個頭啦！」阿釁從抽屜裡抓出一顆鉛筆頭朝溜溜丟過去，「考試又不會因為我們撤退就消失！」\n\n放學的鐘聲，在六年一班頭頂敲響。\n\n如果說月考是暴風雨，那放學後的一系列事件，就是暴風雨前的最後幾聲悶雷。\n\n第一記悶雷，來自校門口。\n\n柯媽媽——家長會副會長、全鎮最會用名牌包敲桌面的媽媽——正堵在接送區，一手拎著手機，一手叉腰，音量比下課鐘還大：\n\n「高老師！我可是看在家長會的面子上，才讓孩子留在六年一班的！這次月考，我們班要是連半個班前十名都沒有，我就把成績單直接寄到教育局！讓全台灣都知道，鹿陽國小六年一班是『補習班救不回的皮蛋班』！」\n\n「柯媽媽，成績是用來評估學習狀況的，不是……」高老師話才說一半。\n\n「我不管評估什麼！我只看分數！」\n\n第二記悶雷，來自聯絡簿。\n\n阿釁在書包裡掏出聯絡簿，翻到最後一頁，看見媽媽用紅筆寫得又粗又大的字：\n\n「阿釁：媽媽把遊戲機收進保險箱了。月考每科都及格，密碼就給你。不及格，暑假送你當職業考生。」\n\n「職業考生是什麼？聽起來好像很威，但仔細想想超恐怖的啊！」阿釁哀號。\n\n第三記悶雷，來自校門外那台載著老巫爸爸的機車。\n\n老巫爸爸一腳踩著機車踏板，一手握著香噴噴的炸雞腿，滿臉得意地晃了晃：\n\n「小巫啊！爸爸跟你打個賭——這次月考你要是每一科都及格，爸爸請你吃一整個月雞腿！要是有一科不及格——嘿嘿，一個月不准碰雞腿，聞都不准聞！」\n\n老巫的臉色瞬間比他的午餐便當還灰白。\n\n「爸，你這樣威脅，跟把我綁在雞腿攤前面餓三天有什麼兩樣！」老巫眼眶泛淚。\n\n「這就是爸爸的愛，懂嗎！」\n\n就在二十六名學生各自被家長的悶雷劈得東倒西歪時，阿釁默默收起了哀嚎，眼神裡燃起一道異樣的光。\n\n他跳上講台，掏出不知道從哪裡撿來的一截粉筆，在黑板正中央用力畫了一個大大的圓：\n\n「各位！聽我說！」\n\n全班的目光「唰」地集中過來。\n\n「月考要到了，家長開火了，主任放話了——大家說，我們是不是只能坐以待斃？」\n\n「是……不然咧？」老巫咬著肉包，滿臉茫然。\n\n「錯！」阿釁在圓圈裡用力點下一個點，「一個人被宰，是意外；二十六個人被宰，是戰役！我宣布——『考試互助會』，現在正式成立！」\n\n「互助會？是要一起複習嗎？」林芸芸怯生生地舉手。\n\n「複習？」阿釁瞪大眼睛，像是聽到了什麼外星語，「芸芸啊，妳太天真了！互助，當然是——你幫我我幫你，大家互相『救』過月考啊！」\n\n空氣安靜了三秒。\n\n老巫第一個反應過來：「所以是……作弊？」\n\n「小聲一點！」阿釁一把摀住老巫的嘴，緊張地瞄了一眼門口，「你是要讓黑面判官第一個來抓我們嗎！」\n\n老巫用力點頭，又用力搖頭，最後點了一下，然後露出一個既害怕又期待的複雜表情。\n\n晴晴坐在第一排，手裡還轉著一把小螺絲起子，冷冷地開口：\n\n「從技術層面來說，全國統一命題的月考，題目沒人看過；除非拿到答案，否則『互助』的實質內容，就是把大家各自記住的部分拼湊起來——這在統計學上，叫做『截長補短』。」\n\n「對！就是這個！晴晴妳真聰明！」阿釁感動得眼眶泛紅，「所以妳加入對不對？」\n\n「我沒說要加入。」晴晴推了推眼鏡，「我只是客觀分析可行性。」\n\n「客觀分析＝加入！妳媽沒教過妳嗎！」阿釁大喜過望，一把抱住晴晴的肩膀。\n\n角落裡，未晞靜靜地站著，左手腕上的時序手環內側微微發光。她溫和地搖了搖頭：\n\n「我不參加。」\n\n阿釁一愣：「未晞，妳成績那麼好，是不需要啦——」\n\n「不是因為成績。」未晞的聲音很輕，卻異常清晰，「是因為……作弊這件事，總有一天要還的。」\n\n「還？還給誰？」阿釁滿頭問號。\n\n未晞沒有回答，只是摸了摸手腕上的光環，眼裡浮現一閃而過的、屬於遙遠未來的陰影。\n\n「總之！」阿釁拍了一下黑板，「考試互助會，二十六人減一人，二十五人成立！從明天起，我們要想出全世界最厲害的作弊方法，讓高老師和周主任都抓不到！」\n\n「可是……」老巫顫抖地舉手，「阿釁，你忘了我們的老師是誰嗎？」\n\n「高老師再強，他也是人嘛！」阿釁豪氣萬丈，「人，就有破綻！」\n\n隔天早自習，阿釁的豪言壯語，就迎來了殘酷的實測。\n\n「各位同學，」高峙舷老師站在講台上，推了推黑框眼鏡，「距離月考還有五天。為了確保考場公平，老師今天就先示範一下——什麼叫做『作弊掃描』。」\n\n他閉上眼睛，再睜開時，鏡片後的瞳孔裡，隱約浮現一圈縮放的金黃色光圈。\n\n下一秒，全班二十六張課桌、二十六個書包、二十六雙手掌心、二十六個鉛筆盒夾層，在他眼底彷彿變成了一張張透明的 X 光片。\n\n「巫茞輆同學，」高老師的目光精準鎖定老巫，「你的橡皮擦左側，用鉛筆寫著『周長＝2πr』，右側寫著『面積＝πr²』。字跡被掌心汗水糊了一半——看來你已經緊張地搓了三天。」\n\n老巫「噗通」一聲從椅子上滑下來，手忙腳亂地把橡皮擦塞進嘴裡，含含糊糊地喊：「老師我沒有！這是我、我、我拿來當護身符的！」\n\n「護身符？」高老師推了推眼鏡，「根據考場規定，護身符若寫有公式，視同作弊工具。巫同學，請你把護身符上的內容，現場背誦一遍，作為誠信練習。」\n\n老巫抖著手把橡皮擦從嘴裡掏出來，看了一眼那幾行被汗水糊得歪歪扭扭的公式，結結巴巴地開口：\n\n「周、周長等於二派ㄚ……圓面積等於派ㄚ平方……」\n\n「很好。」高老師點頭，「字跡雖然模糊，但你背得一字不差。請記住這種感覺——你剛才花了三十秒，就記住了一顆橡皮擦上的全部知識。」\n\n老巫愣住了。\n\n他低頭看看橡皮擦，又抬頭看看黑板，突然發現自己好像真的……記住了？\n\n「接下來，」高老師的目光轉向尪伝恺，「尪同学，你左手掌心上用自動鉛筆寫的三行字，是國語第四課的生字註解。你確定要用這麼容易暈開的位置嗎？」\n\n「噗——！」尪伝恺嚇得直接把手掌往褲子上猛擦。\n\n「林芸芸同學，鉛筆盒夾層裡那張對折的紙，是自然第一單元的重點整理，對嗎？」\n\n林芸芸臉色發白，默默地把鉛筆盒抱進懷裡。\n\n高老師的掃描像一台精密的巡邏衛星，一個一個點名，一個一個拆穿。二十六個人裡，有二十三個身上藏著或大或小的「備用資料」——從橡皮擦、手心、鉛筆盒，到鞋墊底下，無一倖免。\n\n整間教室鴉雀無聲。窗外的溜溜掛在電線上，電子眼瞪得溜圓，尾巴上的毛全部炸開：\n\n「嗶、嗶……目標戰力評估修正：無限大！無限大啊！」\n\n阿釁坐在最後一排，嘴角抽搐。\n\n他原本想說「高老師再強，他也是人」，可現在他看著高老師那雙彷彿能把課桌都看穿的眼睛，第一次覺得——這個老師，可能真的不是人。\n\n「綜合以上，」高老師做結語，「我掃描到了二十三份作弊預備資料。誠實指數：全班百分之十一點五。這個數字，讓我很遺憾。」\n\n全班低著頭，大氣都不敢喘。\n\n「不過，」高老師話鋒一轉，鏡片後的光芒忽然柔和了些，「我發現一件很有意思的事——被掃描到的同學，每一個人都能把自己藏的內容，完整背出來。」\n\n教室裡響起一陣細微的騷動。老巫摸了摸後腦勺：「咦？好像……真的耶？」\n\n「這證明，各位在準備『備用資料』的過程中，其實已經把知識記進腦子裡了。」高老師微微一笑，「各位同學，月考之前，不妨想想這個問題——如果已經記住了，為什麼還要冒著被記過的風險，把它們藏進橡皮擦裡呢？」\n\n放學後，考試互助會第一次正式會議，在教室後排圍成一圈召開。\n\n「各位！」阿釁用力拍桌，「今天大家都看到了！高老師根本不是人！他會透視！會掃描！連鞋墊裡的紙條都逃不過！」\n\n「那……那我們還作弊嗎？」老巫怯生生地問。\n\n「作啊！當然作！」阿釁的眼中燃起熊熊鬥志，「正因為他強，我們才更要作弊！只要我們想出比他更強的作弊方法，就沒人能抓我們！」\n\n「可是阿釁……」晴晴平靜地開口，像是補了一刀，「你剛才也聽到了。高老師說，大家其實都已經把內容記住了。」\n\n「那一定是巧合！」阿釁斬釘截鐵，「什麼『記住了就不用作弊』，這種話只有老實人會信！我可是要拿回遊戲機的男人！」\n\n「還有我的雞腿……」老巫在旁邊小聲補充。\n\n阿釁掏出他那顆撿來的粉筆，在黑板的角落，鄭重地畫下第一個記號：\n\n「從明天開始，我們來想辦法——第一號作弊計畫，正式啟動！」\n\n夜色裡，六年一班的教室悄悄熄了燈。\n\n誰也沒注意到，走廊轉角的陰影處，周嚴主任靜靜放下手中的違規登記簿，嘴角浮起一抹冷笑：\n\n「考試互助會？呵……六年一班，我早就知道你們這群皮蛋不會安分。」\n\n他翻開登記簿，在第一頁空白處，用鋼筆寫下了兩個字：\n\n「盯緊。」","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 1: The Report Card Storm\n\nOn Wednesday afternoon, an announcement more terrifying than a typhoon warning was being held in the classroom of Class 6-1 at Luyang Elementary School.\n\nOn the podium, Teacher Gao Zhixian pushed up his black-rimmed glasses, a faint azure glint flashing in his pupils behind the lenses:\n\n\"Attention, everyone. According to the announcement from the Bureau of Education, the nationwide standardized monthly exam for sixth grade will arrive next Wednesday. Scope: Chinese Lessons 1-5, Math Units 1-4, Science Units 1-3, Social Studies...\"\n\n\"Clank!\"\n\nThe pork bun in Old Wu's mouth dropped straight onto his desk. His eyes went glassy, his voice trembling like a dead leaf in winter:\n\n\"T-Teacher... just hearing the words 'Social Studies' makes me feel like the whole world isn't 'social' anymore...\"\n\nA-Xin collapsed onto his desk, wailing miserably: \"We're doomed! The monthly exam! My mom said if I'm at the bottom of the class again, she'll lock my game console in a safe and make me best friends with a cram school for the whole summer!\"\n\nThat remark was like a lit fuse. All twenty-six faces in the class instantly twisted into bitter gourd shapes.\n\n\"Silence!\"\n\nAt the classroom door, a low, stern voice poured in like a blast of cold air, and the whole class was instantly pressed onto the mute button.\n\nDirector of Student Affairs Zhou Yan strolled in with his hands clasped behind his back, his hawk-sharp gaze sweeping across the class, his infraction notebook already flipped to the newest page:\n\n\"During the exam period, this school will enforce the strictest examination rules in history! Anyone caught with hidden notes, passing papers, or signaling will be penalized in accordance with school regulations! Class 6-1, you little trouble-makers, listen carefully—don't let me, Zhou Yan, see your names on the violation list!\"\n\nNo sooner had Director Zhou left than a mouse-and-fox-like little head poked out of the ceiling ventilation duct with a \"whoosh.\"\n\nLiu-Liu, the class's AI smart pet, flicked its metallic-lustered tail and blinked its electronic eyes with frantic red flashes:\n\n\"Beep beep! Black-Faced Judge intimidation index: ninety-nine! Negative energy blanketing the entire corridor! Recommend the whole class retreat to a safe distance of fifty meters or more!\"\n\n\"Retreat my foot!\" A-Xin grabbed a pencil stub from his drawer and tossed it at Liu-Liu. \"The exam isn't going to disappear just because we retreat!\"\n\nThe dismissal bell rang overhead of Class 6-1.\n\nIf the monthly exam was the storm, then the string of events after school was the last few muffled thunderclaps before the storm.\n\nThe first muffled thunderclap came from the school gate.\n\nMama Ke—vice president of the parent association, and the town's most accomplished mother at slamming tables with designer handbags—was blocking the pickup zone, one hand holding her phone, the other on her hip, her volume louder than the class bell:\n\n\"Teacher Gao! I only let my child stay in Class 6-1 out of respect for the parent association! This time, if our class doesn't even get half a class's worth of students into the top ten, I'll mail the report cards straight to the Bureau of Education! Let all of Taiwan know that Class 6-1 of Luyang Elementary is the 'class of trouble-makers that even cram schools can't save'!\"\n\n\"Mama Ke, grades are meant to assess learning progress, not...\" Teacher Gao barely got half the sentence out.\n\n\"I don't care about assessing anything! I only look at scores!\"\n\nThe second muffled thunderclap came from the home contact notebook.\n\nA-Xin fished the notebook out of his backpack, flipped to the last page, and saw his mother's large, bold words written in red pen:\n\n\"A-Xin: Mom has locked your game console in the safe. Pass every subject on the monthly exam, and I'll give you the password. Fail, and I'll send you to be a professional exam-taker over the summer.\"\n\n\"What's a professional exam-taker? It sounds kind of impressive, but when you think about it, it's terrifying!\" A-Xin wailed.\n\nThe third muffled thunderclap came from the scooter carrying Old Wu's father just outside the school gate.\n\nOld Wu's father, one foot on the scooter pedal, held a fragrant fried chicken drumstick and waved it smugly:\n\n\"Little Wu! Dad wants to make a bet with you—if you pass every subject on this monthly exam, I'll treat you to a whole month of drumsticks! But if you fail even one subject—heh heh, no drumsticks for a month. You can't even smell them!\"\n\nOld Wu's face instantly turned paler than the grayish color of his lunchbox.\n\n\"Dad, threatening me like that is no different from tying me up in front of a drumstick stall and starving me for three days!\" Old Wu said, his eyes welling up.\n\n\"This is a father's love, got it!\"\n\nJust as the twenty-six students were being bowled over by their parents' muffled thunderclaps, A-Xin quietly stopped his wailing, a strange light igniting in his eyes.\n\nHe hopped onto the podium, pulled out a stub of chalk he'd picked up from who-knows-where, and forcefully drew a big circle in the center of the blackboard:\n\n\"Everyone! Listen up!\"\n\nAll eyes in the class snapped over at once.\n\n\"The monthly exam is coming, the parents are opening fire, and the director has laid down the law—tell me, are we just supposed to sit back and wait to be slaughtered?\"\n\n\"Yeah... I guess?\" Old Wu bit into his pork bun, looking utterly lost.\n\n\"Wrong!\" A-Xin stabbed a dot into the center of the circle. \"When one person gets picked off, that's an accident; when twenty-six people get picked off, that's a battle! I hereby declare—the 'Exam Mutual Aid Society' is now officially established!\"\n\n\"A mutual aid society? Is it for studying together?\" Lin Yunyun timidly raised her hand.\n\n\"Studying?\" A-Xin widened his eyes as if he'd just heard some alien language. \"Yunyun, you're so naive! Mutual aid is, of course—you help me, I help you, everyone 'rescues' each other through the monthly exam!\"\n\nThe air fell silent for three seconds.\n\nOld Wu was the first to react: \"So it's... cheating?\"\n\n\"Keep your voice down!\" A-Xin clapped a hand over Old Wu's mouth, glancing nervously at the doorway. \"Do you want the Black-Faced Judge to be the first one to catch us?!\"\n\nOld Wu nodded hard, then shook his head hard, then nodded once more, finally flashing a complicated expression that was equal parts scared and excited.\n\nQingqing sat in the first row, twirling a small screwdriver in her hand, speaking coolly:\n\n\"From a technical standpoint, the questions on a nationally standardized monthly exam have never been seen by anyone. Unless we get the answer key, the real substance of 'mutual aid' is just stitching together whatever bits each of us remembers—which, in statistics, is called 'cutting the long to patch the short.'\"\n\n\"Yes! That's exactly it! Qingqing, you're so smart!\" A-Xin said, his eyes welling with emotion. \"So you're joining, right?\"\n\n\"I didn't say I'd join.\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses. \"I was just objectively analyzing the feasibility.\"\n\n\"Objective analysis = joining! Didn't your mom ever teach you that?!\" A-Xin, overjoyed, threw his arm around Qingqing's shoulders.\n\nIn the corner, Weixi stood quietly, the inside of the chrono bracelet on her left wrist glowing faintly. She shook her head gently:\n\n\"I'm not joining.\"\n\nA-Xin was taken aback: \"Weixi, with grades as good as yours, you don't need to—\"\n\n\"It's not about the grades.\" Weixi's voice was very soft, yet extraordinarily clear. \"It's because... cheating is something that will have to be paid back someday.\"\n\n\"Paid back? To whom?\" A-Xin was full of question marks.\n\nWeixi didn't answer. She only touched the glowing ring on her wrist, a fleeting shadow from a distant future flickering across her eyes.\n\n\"Anyway!\" A-Xin clapped the blackboard. \"The Exam Mutual Aid Society—twenty-six members minus one, that's twenty-five, officially established! Starting tomorrow, we're going to come up with the most amazing cheating methods in the whole world, so powerful that neither Teacher Gao nor Director Zhou can catch us!\"\n\n\"But...\" Old Wu raised his hand timidly. \"A-Xin, have you forgotten who our teacher is?\"\n\n\"No matter how strong Teacher Gao is, he's still human!\" A-Xin declared with heroic bravado. \"And humans have weaknesses!\"\n\nThe next morning, during morning self-study, A-Xin's grand declaration met its ruthless live test.\n\n\"Classmates,\" Teacher Gao Zhixian stood on the podium, pushing up his black-rimmed glasses, \"there are still five days until the monthly exam. To ensure fairness on the exam, today I'll demonstrate firsthand—what is called a 'cheating scan.'\"\n\nHe closed his eyes, and when he opened them again, a golden ring of light appeared faintly in his pupils, zooming and shrinking.\n\nIn the next second, twenty-six desks, twenty-six backpacks, twenty-six palms, and twenty-six pencil-case compartments all became transparent X-ray plates beneath his gaze.\n\n\"Wu Chenkai,\" Teacher Gao's gaze locked precisely onto Old Wu, \"on the left side of your eraser is written 'circumference = 2πr,' and on the right side 'area = πr².' Half of the writing is smudged by the sweat on your palm—it looks like you've been nervously rubbing it for three days.\"\n\nOld Wu slid right off his chair with a \"thump,\" frantically stuffing the eraser into his mouth and mumbling: \"Teacher, I didn't! This is, this is, I'm using it as a talisman!\"\n\n\"A talisman?\" Teacher Gao pushed up his glasses. \"According to examination rules, a talisman with formulas written on it is treated as a cheating tool. Mr. Wu, please recite the contents of your talisman aloud, right here, as an honesty exercise.\"\n\nOld Wu, hands trembling, fished the eraser out of his mouth. Glancing at the formulas smeared crookedly by sweat, he stammered:\n\n\"The circ-circumference equals two pi r... the circle's area equals pi r squared...\"\n\n\"Very good.\" Teacher Gao nodded. \"The writing is blurry, but you recited it perfectly. Remember this feeling—in thirty seconds just now, you absorbed all the knowledge that was on one eraser.\"\n\nOld Wu was stunned.\n\nHe looked down at the eraser, then up at the blackboard, and suddenly realized that maybe he had really... remembered it?\n\n\"Next,\" Teacher Gao's gaze turned to Wang Zhuankai, \"on the palm of your left hand, written in mechanical pencil, are three lines of annotations from Lesson 4 of Chinese. Are you sure you want to put them somewhere that smudges so easily?\"\n\n\"Pfft!\" Wang Zhuankai, frightened, frantically wiped his palm against his pants.\n\n\"Lin Yunyun, the folded paper in your pencil case—that's your review notes for Science Unit 1, isn't it?\"\n\nLin Yunyun turned pale, silently hugging her pencil case to her chest.\n\nTeacher Gao's scan was like a precise patrol satellite, naming one student after another, exposing one scheme after another. Out of the twenty-six students, twenty-three had hidden \"backup materials\" of varying sizes on them—from erasers, palms, and pencil cases, all the way down to the soles of their shoes. None escaped.\n\nThe entire classroom was dead silent. Liu-Liu hung on the wire outside the window, electronic eyes wide as saucers, all the fur on its tail bristling:\n\n\"Beep, beep... target combat assessment revision: infinite! Absolutely infinite!\"\n\nA-Xin sat in the last row, the corners of his mouth twitching.\n\nHe had originally wanted to say \"no matter how strong Teacher Gao is, he's still human,\" but now, watching Teacher Gao's eyes that seemed able to see straight through the desks, he felt for the first time—this teacher might really not be human.\n\n\"To sum up,\" Teacher Gao concluded, \"I scanned twenty-three sets of prepared cheating materials. Honesty index: eleven and a half percent for the whole class. This number makes me very sorry to hear.\"\n\nThe whole class lowered their heads, not daring to breathe.\n\n\"However,\" Teacher Gao shifted his tone, the light behind his lenses suddenly softening, \"I discovered something very interesting—every student who was scanned can recite the contents they were hiding, completely.\"\n\nA faint stir rippled through the classroom. Old Wu scratched the back of his head: \"Huh? It seems... really, yeah?\"\n\n\"This proves that, in the process of preparing their 'backup materials,' you all actually already stored the knowledge in your heads.\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly. \"Classmates, before the monthly exam, consider this question—if you've already remembered it, why risk getting written up to hide it inside an eraser?\"\n\nAfter school, the first formal meeting of the Exam Mutual Aid Society was convened in a circle at the back of the classroom.\n\n\"Everyone!\" A-Xin slapped the table hard. \"We all saw it today! Teacher Gao is not human at all! He can see through things! He can scan! Even a note in the sole of your shoe can't escape!\"\n\n\"So... so should we still cheat?\" Old Wu asked timidly.\n\n\"Cheat! Of course we'll cheat!\" The fighting spirit blazed in A-Xin's eyes. \"Precisely because he's so strong, we have to cheat even more! As long as we come up with a cheating method stronger than his detection, nobody can catch us!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin...\" Qingqing spoke calmly, as if delivering a finishing blow. \"You heard it just now. Teacher Gao said everyone has actually already remembered the material.\"\n\n\"That must be a coincidence!\" A-Xin said firmly. \"Stuff like 'once you remember it, you don't need to cheat'—only goody-goodies believe that! I'm a man who's getting his game console back!\"\n\n\"And my drumsticks...\" Old Wu added quietly on the side.\n\nA-Xin pulled out the chalk stub he'd picked up and, at the corner of the blackboard, solemnly drew the first tally mark:\n\n\"Starting tomorrow, we'll figure out a way—Cheating Plan No. 1, officially launched!\"\n\nNight fell, and the classroom of Class 6-1 quietly went dark.\n\nNobody noticed that, in the shadows at the corner of the hallway, Director Zhou Yan quietly set down his infraction notebook, a cold smile curling at the corner of his mouth:\n\n\"Exam Mutual Aid Society? Hmph... Class 6-1, I've known all along that you little trouble-makers wouldn't stay quiet.\"\n\nHe flipped open his notebook and, on the blank first page, wrote two words in pen:\n\n\"Keep a close watch.\""},{"id":2,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第二章：橡皮擦上的微型圖書館\n\n放學後的六年一班教室，窗簾拉得密不透風，燈關了一半。\n\n教室後排的課桌上，二十六本聯絡簿堆成一座小山，阿釁站在桌子正中央，手裡捏著一截粉筆，像指揮官一樣環視全場：\n\n「各位！昨天的掃描大家都看到了！高老師那雙眼睛，連鞋墊裡藏紙條都看得見！」\n\n「那……那我們還作弊嗎？」老巫舉手，聲音發抖。\n\n「作！當然作！」阿釁眼中燃起熊熊鬥志，「正因為他強，我們才要比他更強！昨天他掃出二十三份『備用資料』，那是因為——大家準備得太粗糙了！」\n\n他轉身，在黑板上用力寫下幾個大字：\n\n**「第一號計畫：微型圖書館」**\n\n「各位！傳統的小抄，又大又容易漏餡！所以我們要把重點濃縮、濃縮、再濃縮，縮到『藏在哪裡都不起眼』的地步！讓高老師就算透視，也找不到！」\n\n「可是阿釁……」晴晴推了推眼鏡，語氣平靜得像在念氣象報告，「你昨天親眼看到，高老師連橡皮擦上糊掉的鉛筆字都掃得出來。你覺得『縮小』有用嗎？」\n\n「晴晴，這就是妳不懂了！」阿釁雙手叉腰，「昨天是『個人零散準備』，今天我們是『全班系統化作戰』！單打獨鬥打不過，集團作戰總行了吧！」\n\n「從統計學上來說……」晴晴正要開口。\n\n「閉嘴！統計學這次聽我的！」阿釁一把搶過話筒。\n\n於是，「考試互助會」的第一次系統化作業，正式展開。\n\n阿釁把全班二十六人分成四組，每組認領一科：\n\n「國語組——把每課生字註解縮成三行！」\n「數學組——所有公式、單位換算，縮成一張名片大小！」\n「自然組——實驗步驟、重點整理，一律用代號！」\n「社會組——地名、年代、人物，全部濃縮！」\n\n「報告！」老巫舉手，「濃縮之後，要放在哪裡？」\n\n「這還用問？」阿釁神秘一笑，「各位——請看！」\n\n他從書包裡掏出一堆零零碎碎的小東西：橡皮擦、鉛筆、尺、墊板、自動筆芯盒、修正帶、指甲油瓶……每一樣上面，都貼著一張寫了字的標籤。\n\n「這就是我們班的『微型圖書館』！」阿釁得意地宣布，「橡皮擦＝數學館！墊板＝自然館！鉛筆盒夾層＝國語館！手掌心＝社會館！每一本書，都藏在最不起眼的地方！」\n\n「可是阿釁，」林芸芸怯生生地舉手，「這麼小的字，誰寫得出來啊？」\n\n「這就要靠我們的技術總監了！」\n\n阿釁「啪」地把一支筆頭細得像針尖的工程筆拍在晴晴桌上：\n\n「晴晴！交棒給妳了！」\n\n「我拒絕。」晴晴斬釘截鐵，「我只負責研究，不負責使用。」\n\n「誰要妳用了？」阿釁瞪大眼睛，「我是要妳『製作』！製作不等於使用！這是科學家的天職！」\n\n「……你這種歪理，怎麼聽起來好像有點道理。」晴晴嘆了口氣，終究還是拿起工程筆，架好放大鏡，戴上奶奶的老花眼鏡，開始在一塊塊橡皮擦上，用筆尖雕琢出螞蟻大小的字。\n\n「哇——！」老巫湊過去一看，嚇得往後一跌，「晴晴！妳這字，比我爸的簽名還小！」\n\n「這就是重點。」晴晴頭也不抬，「小到高老師的透視光眼，都會忽略它的存在。」\n\n「好！很好！」阿釁滿意地點頭，「各位，我們來分配角色！老巫，你是『頭號客戶』，明天自然小考，你第一個上場實測！」\n\n「我、我第一個？」老巫嚇得把肉包整顆塞進嘴裡，「為什麼是我？」\n\n「因為你最需要啊！」阿釁拍拍他的肩，「考得好，雞腿就是你的！」\n\n老巫的眼神從恐懼，慢慢變成一種壯烈的堅定：「……好！為了雞腿！我、我拼了！」\n\n深夜十點，六年一班的教室燈終於熄了。\n\n黑暗裡，溜溜從通風管探出頭，電子眼掃過那一桌子的「微型圖書館」，發出一聲憂慮的電子嗶聲：\n\n「嗶嗶……偵測到大量高風險物品……根據歷史資料，這類物品的平均存活時間：一個早上。」\n\n隔天早自習，自然課的小考鈴聲響起前，老巫握著他那塊寫滿公式的橡皮擦，額頭上全是汗。\n\n「老巫，自然小考都是選擇題，你只要記得這三題的重點就好——光合作用！氣體交換！植物分類！」阿釁低聲叮囑。\n\n「可是阿釁，我緊張……」老巫的手在發抖。\n\n「緊張什麼！你可是要拿回雞腿的男人！」阿釁用力拍拍他的肩，然後迅速坐回自己的座位。\n\n小考開始。\n\n考卷發下來，老巫顫抖著拿起筆，偷偷瞄了一眼桌上的橡皮擦。\n\n——很好，公式清清楚楚！\n\n他正要低頭抄寫——\n\n「巫茞輆同學。」\n\n高峙舷老師的聲音，像一道驚雷，在老巫頭頂炸開。\n\n老巫整個人僵在原地，橡皮擦「啪」地從他手裡滑落，滾到講台前，精準地停在高老師的皮鞋尖下。\n\n「看來……」高老師彎腰，用兩根手指優雅地拾起橡皮擦，對著晨光端詳了一下，「這座『微型圖書館』的『數學館』，今天開張了？」\n\n全班的臉，瞬間全部刷白。\n\n「還有——」高老師的目光掃過全班，鏡片後的瞳孔浮現一圈金色的光圈，「國語館、自然館、社會館……以及各位手上的『掌上書庫』，都開張了吧？」\n\n他閉上眼睛，再睜開：\n\n「巫同學，橡皮擦左側是數學公式；尪伝恺同學，你的左手小指指甲上，用修正液寫了三個字；林芸芸同學，鉛筆盒夾層的紙片，上面是自然重點——以及，全班二十六人的手上，都殘留著同一種特殊墨水。」\n\n晴晴的筆「咔噠」一聲掉在地上。\n\n「那種墨水的成分，是從工程筆芯調製的特殊配比。」高老師緩緩走下講台，走到晴晴桌前，微微低頭，鏡片後的光芒直直落在她身上，「全校只有一個人，會用這種比例的墨寫字。綝耘晴同學——妳可以解釋一下，為什麼全班的手上，都有妳的『筆跡』嗎？」\n\n晴晴張了張嘴，最後，她閉上眼睛，語氣平靜得像在交作業：\n\n「報告老師。我只負責製作，不負責使用。」\n\n「很好。」高老師點點頭，「那我們來談談『製作』的部分。」\n\n就在全班以為要集體陣亡的時候——\n\n「砰！」\n\n教室門被一把推開，周嚴主任大步流星地衝了進來，鷹隼般的目光掃過全班：\n\n「我剛剛在走廊就看到這孩子鬼鬼祟祟地看橡皮擦！抓到了吧！違規登記簿我都準備好了！」\n\n他得意地揚了揚手裡的登記簿，卻看見全班二十六個人，都用一種「你來得太晚了」的表情看著他。\n\n周嚴愣住了：「……怎麼回事？」\n\n「周主任。」高老師轉身，面色平靜，「巫同學剛才正在進行『誠信練習』——背誦橡皮擦上的公式，確認自己確實記住了。這是教育部推廣的『主動記憶法』。」\n\n「主、主動記憶法？」\n\n「您看，」高老師把橡皮擦舉到周嚴眼前，「這上面寫的，是巫同學自己整理的重點。他不但背得出來，而且背得一字不差。這正是『整理重點、反覆記憶』的最佳示範。」\n\n周嚴瞪大眼睛，左看看橡皮擦，右看看滿頭大汗的老巫，再看看氣定神閒的高老師，最後，他把登記簿「唰」地合上：\n\n「哼……算、算你們走運！記住，月考要是讓我抓到，就不是背橡皮擦這麼簡單了！」\n\n他悻悻然地摔門離去。\n\n周嚴一走，教室裡響起一陣虛脫的喘息聲。老巫癱在椅子上，整個人像被抽乾了力氣。\n\n「各位同學，」高老師重新走上講台，語氣卻意外地緩和，「剛才的『微型圖書館』，設計得很用心。橡皮擦、墊板、指甲，每一處都藏得很巧妙——如果能用在對的地方，這其實是一份很棒的『重點整理』。」\n\n他走下講台，把沒收的橡皮擦、墊板、鉛筆盒夾層紙片，一一整齊地排在黑板上：\n\n「所以，這些『藏書』，從今天起，就正式捐給全班——貼在黑板旁的公布欄上，成為我們的『複習專區』。任何同學想看，隨時都可以看。」\n\n「捐……捐出來？」阿釁張大嘴巴。\n\n「這就是老師說的『用在對的地方』。」高老師微微一笑，鏡片閃過一道光，「巫同學，你剛才那場小考，答對了幾題？」\n\n「呃……」老巫低頭看了看自己的考卷，愣了好幾秒，「好像……全部答對了？」\n\n「因為你背下橡皮擦上的公式了。」高老師說，「記住了，就不用再看橡皮擦——這句話，我上週就說過了。」\n\n教室裡一片安靜。\n\n老巫呆呆地看著自己那份全對的小考卷，再看看公布欄上那塊被捐出去的橡皮擦，突然發現一件很奇怪的事：\n\n「奇怪……我怎麼覺得，我好像從昨天開始，數學就莫名變好了？」\n\n「那就是你的錯覺！」阿釁「啪」地一拍桌子站起來，滿臉不甘心，「各位！失敗一次不算什麼！高老師有透視光眼，那我們就躲過他的眼睛！我宣布——第二號計畫，明天開始！」\n\n「可是阿釁……」晴晴慢悠悠地補了一句，「你剛剛才親眼看到，全班用『微型圖書館』，把小考全部考對了。我們到底……為什麼還要作弊？」\n\n阿釁愣在原地，張了張嘴，卻一句話也答不出來。\n\n窗外的溜溜從通風管探出頭，甩了甩尾巴，用只有自己聽得到的電子音，小聲嘀咕：\n\n「嗶嗶……數據統計顯示：人類的固執，果然是所有物種裡最高的……」","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 2: The Miniature Library on an Eraser\n\nAfter school, the curtains in the classroom of Class 6-1 were drawn tight, and half the lights were turned off.\n\nTwenty-six contact notebooks were piled into a small mountain on the desks in the back row. A-Xin stood on top of the desk, chalk in hand, scanning the room like a commander:\n\n\"Everyone! You all saw yesterday's scan! Teacher Gao's pair of eyes can see even a paper note hidden in the sole of your shoe!\"\n\n\"So... so should we still cheat?\" Old Wu raised his hand, his voice trembling.\n\n\"Cheat! Of course we'll cheat!\" The fighting spirit blazed in A-Xin's eyes. \"Precisely because he's so strong, we have to be stronger! Yesterday he scanned out twenty-three 'backup materials'—that's because everyone prepared too crudely!\"\n\nHe turned and wrote several large words on the blackboard:\n\n**\"Plan No. 1: Miniature Library\"**\n\n\"Everyone! Traditional cheat sheets are big and easy to expose! So we have to concentrate, concentrate, concentrate—concentrate the material until it's 'hidden anywhere and looks like nothing'! Even if Teacher Gao uses his X-ray vision, he won't find it!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin...\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses, her tone as calm as a weather report, \"you saw with your own eyes yesterday that Teacher Gao can scan even the blurred pencil words on an eraser. Do you really think 'making it smaller' will work?\"\n\n\"Qingqing, that's where you don't get it!\" A-Xin put his hands on his hips. \"Yesterday was 'scattered individual preparation'; today is 'whole-class systematic warfare'! If we can't win fighting solo, we'll win fighting as a team!\"\n\n\"From a statistical standpoint...\" Qingqing began.\n\n\"Shut up! This time, statistics listens to me!\" A-Xin snatched the conversation.\n\nAnd so, the first systematic operation of the Exam Mutual Aid Society officially began.\n\nA-Xin divided the whole class of twenty-six into four groups, each claiming one subject:\n\n\"Chinese group—condense each lesson's new-word annotations into three lines!\"\n\"Math group—shrink all formulas and unit conversions to the size of a business card!\"\n\"Science group—use code names for experiments and key points!\"\n\"Social group—condense all the place names, dates, and people!\"\n\n\"Reporting!\" Old Wu raised his hand. \"After we condense them, where do we put them?\"\n\n\"Now that's the right question!\" A-Xin smiled mysteriously. \"Everyone—take a look!\"\n\nHe pulled a pile of odds and ends out of his backpack: erasers, pencils, rulers, desk pads, mechanical-lead boxes, correction tape, a bottle of nail polish... and each one had a label stuck on it.\n\n\"This is our class's 'Miniature Library'!\" A-Xin announced proudly. \"Eraser = Math Library! Desk pad = Science Library! Pencil case = Chinese Library! Palm = Social Library! Every book is hidden in the least conspicuous place!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin,\" Lin Yunyun timidly raised her hand, \"who can possibly write letters that small?\"\n\n\"That's what our tech director is for!\"\n\nA-Xin \"slapped\" an engineering pen with a needle-fine tip onto Qingqing's desk:\n\n\"Qingqing! Handing the baton to you!\"\n\n\"I refuse.\" Qingqing said flatly. \"I only research, I don't use.\"\n\n\"Who said you'd use it?\" A-Xin widened his eyes. \"I mean you 'make' it! Making isn't using! That's a scientist's sacred duty!\"\n\n\"...Your twisted logic somehow sounds kind of reasonable.\" Qingqing sighed, and in the end, she picked up the engineering pen, set up the magnifier, put on her grandmother's reading glasses, and began carving ant-sized characters onto erasers under the lens.\n\n\"Wow!\" Old Wu leaned in to look, then stumbled backward. \"Qingqing! Your writing is smaller than my dad's signature!\"\n\n\"That's the point.\" Qingqing didn't look up. \"Small enough that Teacher Gao's X-ray vision will overlook its existence.\"\n\n\"Good! Very good!\" A-Xin nodded with satisfaction. \"Everyone, let's assign roles! Old Wu, you're 'Customer No. 1'—tomorrow's science quiz, you test it first!\"\n\n\"M-Me first?\" Old Wu stuffed a whole pork bun into his mouth. \"Why me?\"\n\n\"Because you need it the most!\" A-Xin patted his shoulder. \"Pass, and the drumsticks are yours!\"\n\nOld Wu's eyes shifted from fear to a kind of heroic resolve: \"...Fine! For the drumsticks! I'll do it!\"\n\nAt ten o'clock that night, the lights in the classroom of Class 6-1 finally went out.\n\nIn the darkness, Liu-Liu poked its head out of the ventilation duct, its electronic eyes sweeping over the table full of \"Miniature Library\" items, letting out a worried electronic beep:\n\n\"Beep beep... detecting a large quantity of high-risk items... according to historical data, the average survival time of this type of item: one morning.\"\n\nThe next morning, before the bell for the science quiz, Old Wu gripped the eraser covered with formulas, sweat beading on his forehead.\n\n\"Old Wu, the science quiz is all multiple choice. You just need to remember three key points—photosynthesis! gas exchange! plant classification!\" A-Xin whispered urgently.\n\n\"But A-Xin, I'm nervous...\" Old Wu's hand was shaking.\n\n\"Nervous about what! You're the man who's getting his drumsticks back!\" A-Xin patted him firmly, then quickly returned to his own seat.\n\nThe quiz began.\n\nAs the test papers were handed out, Old Wu picked up his pen with trembling hands and secretly glanced at the eraser on his desk.\n\n—The formulas were all right there, clear as day!\n\nHe was just about to lower his head and copy them down—\n\n\"Wu Chenkai.\"\n\nTeacher Gao Zhixian's voice exploded like a clap of thunder directly above Old Wu's head.\n\nOld Wu froze on the spot. The eraser \"slapped\" out of his hand, rolled to the front of the podium, and stopped precisely at the toe of Teacher Gao's leather shoe.\n\n\"It seems...\" Teacher Gao bent down, elegantly picking up the eraser with two fingers and examining it against the light, \"the 'Math Library' of this 'Miniature Library' has opened for business today?\"\n\nThe faces of the entire class turned white in an instant.\n\n\"And—\" Teacher Gao's gaze swept across the class, a golden ring appearing in his pupils behind the lenses, \"the Chinese Library, the Science Library, the Social Library... as well as the 'palm book vaults' in your hands—they've all opened for business too, haven't they?\"\n\nHe closed his eyes, then opened them again:\n\n\"Mr. Wu, math formulas on the left side of the eraser; Wang Zhuankai, three characters written in correction fluid on the pinky nail of your left hand; Lin Yunyun, the paper in your pencil case, science key points—and, everyone in the class is carrying traces of the same special ink on their hands.\"\n\nQingqing's pen \"clicked\" and fell to the floor.\n\n\"That ink is blended from a special ratio of engineering-pen core.\" Teacher Gao slowly stepped off the podium, walked to Qingqing's desk, lowered his head, the light behind his lenses falling straight on her. \"There is exactly one person in this whole school who writes with that ratio of ink. Lin Yunqing—can you explain why the hands of the entire class all carry your 'handwriting'?\"\n\nQingqing opened her mouth, then finally closed her eyes, her tone as calm as if she were handing in homework:\n\n\"Reporting to the teacher. I only make them. I don't use them.\"\n\n\"Very good.\" Teacher Gao nodded. \"Then let's talk about the 'making' part.\"\n\nJust as the whole class thought they were all going to go down together—\n\n\"Bang!\"\n\nThe classroom door was pushed open, and Director Zhou Yan strode in, his hawk-sharp gaze sweeping the room:\n\n\"I just saw this kid sneakily staring at his eraser from the hallway! Caught red-handed! I've already got my infraction notebook ready!\"\n\nHe smugly waved his notebook—only to see all twenty-six students looking at him with expressions that clearly said \"you came too late.\"\n\nDirector Zhou froze: \"...What's going on?\"\n\n\"Director Zhou.\" Teacher Gao turned, his expression calm. \"Mr. Wu was just performing an 'honesty exercise'—reciting the formulas on his eraser to confirm he truly remembered them. This is the 'active memorization method' promoted by the Ministry of Education.\"\n\n\"Act-Active memorization method?\"\n\n\"Look,\" Teacher Gao held the eraser up in front of Director Zhou, \"written here are Mr. Wu's own organized key points. Not only can he recite them, he recites them perfectly. This is a textbook demonstration of 'organizing key points and memorizing through repetition.'\"\n\nDirector Zhou stared wide-eyed, glancing left at the eraser, right at the sweat-soaked Old Wu, then back at the imperturbable Gao in the middle. Finally, he \"snapped\" his notebook shut:\n\n\"Hmph... consider yourselves lucky! But remember—if I catch you on the monthly exam, it won't be as simple as reciting an eraser!\"\n\nHe stormed off, slamming the door.\n\nNo sooner had Director Zhou left than the classroom let out a collective sigh of relief. Old Wu collapsed into his chair, looking as if every last drop of strength had been drained from him.\n\n\"Everyone,\" Teacher Gao returned to the podium, his tone unexpectedly gentle, \"that 'Miniature Library' was very thoughtfully designed. The eraser, the desk pad, the fingernail—every hiding place was clever. If you could use this ability in the right place, it would actually be a wonderful piece of 'key-point organization.'\"\n\nHe stepped down from the podium and laid the confiscated eraser, desk pad, and pencil-case paper in a neat row on the blackboard:\n\n\"So these 'hidden books,' starting today, are officially donated to the whole class—posted on the bulletin board beside the blackboard, becoming our 'review zone.' Any student may look at them anytime.\"\n\n\"Do-Donated?\" A-Xin's mouth fell open.\n\n\"This is what the teacher meant by 'used in the right place.'\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly, a glint flashing across his lenses. \"Mr. Wu, how many questions did you answer correctly on that quiz just now?\"\n\n\"Uh...\" Old Wu looked down at his own quiz paper and froze for a few seconds. \"It seems... I got all of them right?\"\n\n\"Because you memorized the formulas on the eraser.\" Teacher Gao said. \"Remember, once you've memorized it, you don't need to look at the eraser—I said that last week.\"\n\nThe classroom fell silent.\n\nOld Wu stared blankly at his all-correct quiz paper, then at the donated eraser on the bulletin board, and suddenly discovered something very strange:\n\n\"Strange... why do I feel like... my math has been getting better for no reason since yesterday?\"\n\n\"That's your illusion!\" A-Xin \"slapped\" the table and stood up, refusing to accept it. \"Everyone! Failing once means nothing! Teacher Gao has X-ray vision, so we'll just stay out of his eyes! I declare—Plan No. 2 starts tomorrow!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin...\" Qingqing slowly added, a hint of a sting in her words, \"you just watched the whole class get every quiz answer right using the 'Miniature Library,' with your own eyes. So... why do we still need to cheat?\"\n\nA-Xin stood frozen on the spot, opening his mouth, yet unable to answer even a single word.\n\nOutside the window, Liu-Liu poked its head out of the ventilation duct, flicked its tail, and muttered in a tiny electronic voice that only it could hear:\n\n\"Beep beep... statistics show: human stubbornness is, indeed, the highest among all species...\""},{"id":3,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第三章：紙飛機與橡皮筋傳送帶\n\n「各位！微型圖書館陣亡了！」\n\n放學後的教室裡，阿釁把一枝粉筆用力折成兩截，滿臉憤慨地拍在講台上：\n\n「但是，失敗不代表結束！高老師有透視光眼，那我們就——不藏了！改成『運』的！」\n\n「運？運什麼？」老巫嘴裡含著肉包，含糊地問。\n\n「運——答案！」阿釁在黑板上用力畫出三個大字，「第二號計畫：空中傳輸系統！」\n\n他展開一張寫滿鬼畫符的設計圖，上面畫著密密麻麻的箭頭、虛線和不明所以的圓圈：\n\n「各位請看！與其讓每個人都冒著被掃描的風險藏小抄，不如讓我們當中最聰明的人負責『知道答案』，再把答案——空投給大家！」\n\n「所以我們要一個『主機』？」晴晴推了推眼鏡。\n\n「對！主機就是——」阿釁的目光在全班掃了一圈，最後落在第一排那個正低頭寫作業的少女身上，「未晞！」\n\n林未晞抬起頭，眼裡帶著淡淡的疑惑：「我？」\n\n「妳成績最好啊！」阿釁湊過去，雙手合十，「未晞，只要妳在模擬考上把答案傳給大家，全班就有救了！」\n\n「我不作弊。」未晞的回答乾淨俐落。\n\n「可是……」\n\n「而且，」未晞輕輕搖了搖頭，「阿釁，答案這種東西，用『傳』的，一定會有傳錯、傳漏、傳慢的一天。真正可靠的，只有自己腦子裡那套。」\n\n「那是因為妳腦子好啊！」阿釁抱頭哀嚎。\n\n「那你就——讓大家的腦子，也變好。」未晞溫和地留下這句話，低頭繼續寫作業。\n\n「好！你不當主機，我們自己造！」阿釁轉向全班，指著設計圖，「空投系統，三路並進！第一路——紙飛機！第二路——橡皮筋彈射！第三路——粉筆盒空投，由溜溜親自駕駛！」\n\n「嗶？」溜溜從通風管探出頭，電子眼裡寫滿「關我屁事」。\n\n「溜溜！這是全班託付給你的重責大任！」阿釁拿出一罐潤滑油，在溜溜面前晃了晃，「任務成功，這罐『頂級太空潤滑油』就是你的！」\n\n溜溜的電子眼瞬間亮得像兩顆小太陽，尾巴高高豎起，發出亢奮的電子音：\n\n「嗶嗶嗶！收到！溜溜航空，隨時準備起飛！」\n\n「好！全員動工！」\n\n於是，「考試互助會」的地下工廠，熱火朝天地開工了。\n\n尪伝恺負責摺紙飛機。他一連摺了十幾架，每一架都歪歪扭扭，有的機翼一長一短，有的機頭像被踩過一樣扁塌。阿釁看了半天，忍不住吐槽：\n\n「你這飛機，飛得起來嗎？」\n\n「飛不飛得起來是一回事，」尪伝恺自信滿滿，「重點是——帥！」\n\n「帥？你這是『帥』？我看是『衰』吧！」阿釁無力地扶額。\n\n另一邊，老巫正對著一條粗橡皮筋發愁。他把橡皮筋套在手指上，用力一拉——「咻」地一聲，橡皮筋彈了出去，精準地打中了一張紙飛機，把機頭打成了兩半。\n\n「哇！老巫！你這是彈射還是破壞啊！」阿釁跳起來大喊。\n\n「我、我這是在測試力道！」老巫委屈地揉著手指，「誰知道它這麼有力……」\n\n「你拿我自己摺的飛機來試！」尪伝恺心疼地捧著殘骸。\n\n角落裡，晴晴默默地組裝著第三路系統——粉筆盒空投艙。她拆了三個粉筆盒，用膠帶綁成一個簡易吊艙，中間掛著溜溜的專屬安全帶，前後還裝了兩片用尺子削成的平衡翼。\n\n「空投艙完成。」晴晴推了推眼鏡，「理論上，溜溜攜帶答案紙起飛，飛到目標上空，鬆開吊艙，答案紙就會精準落在指定位置。誤差估計：三公分以內。」\n\n「誤差三公分？」阿釁瞪大眼睛，「那不就是『掉在老巫的肉包上』的距離嗎？」\n\n「正是。」晴晴平靜地點頭，「所以我把目標設定為——老巫的桌子正中央。」\n\n「為什麼是我？」老巫慘叫。\n\n「因為你是頭號客戶。」晴晴頭也不抬。\n\n隔天，月考前的全校模擬考，準時登場。\n\n考卷發下來，阿釁坐在第一排，他是「答案傳遞中繼站」；老巫坐在第五排，他是「頭號客戶」；窗外，溜溜叼著一張寫滿答案的紙，已經在屋簷上就位。\n\n「各位！」阿釁在心裡默唸，「成敗在此一舉！三路空投，總有一路成功！」\n\n「啾——」\n\n第一路，紙飛機出動。\n\n尪伝恺把他精心摺出的「帥氣戰機」往斜後方一丟，紙飛機拖著一條歪斜的弧線，搖搖晃晃地朝老巫飛去——\n\n「啪。」\n\n兩根手指在半空中，穩穩夾住了紙飛機的機翼。\n\n高峙舷老師站在講台上，鏡片後的瞳孔浮現一圈金色的光圈，語氣平淡得像在宣布天氣：\n\n「尪伝恺同學，你這架紙飛機的飛行參數：初速度每秒二點一公尺，仰角三十一度，受到講台電扇氣流的干擾，會偏離目標方向四十五度。順帶一提——就算它成功降落，上面的字，也不是你要的答案。」\n\n全班倒抽一口涼氣。\n\n「三D空間軌跡追蹤系統啟動。」高老師推了推眼鏡，「各位同學，請不要考驗老師的計算能力。」\n\n阿釁咬緊牙關：「沒關係！還有第二路！」\n\n老巫顫抖著把橡皮筋套上手指，對準阿釁的方向，用力一拉——「咻——」橡皮筋夾著一張摺成小方塊的答案紙，呼嘯而出！\n\n「啪！」\n\n又被夾住了。\n\n高老師連頭都沒轉，隨手一抬，橡皮筋上的紙條就被他精準地攔截在指縫間，同時橡皮筋彈回來，「啪」地打在老巫自己的額頭上，留下一個紅紅的印子。\n\n「巫同學，」高老師嘆了一口氣，「你這條橡皮筋，彈性模數零點八，回彈率百分之九十三——打中你自己的機率，比打中我高出六倍。」\n\n「嗚……」老巫捂著額頭，眼眶泛淚。\n\n「還有最後一路！」阿釁把心一橫，發出暗號，「溜溜！上！」\n\n窗外，溜溜叼著裝滿答案紙的粉筆盒吊艙，像一枚銀白色的小火箭，從屋簷俯衝而下！牠的耳朵壓低，尾巴在空氣中甩出一道漂亮的弧線，精準地朝老巫的桌子俯衝——\n\n「溜溜航空，最後衝刺！」\n\n「咻——！」\n\n就在吊艙即將抵達目標的瞬間，高老師的右手以一種違反人體工學的速度探出，一把抓住空中的吊艙吊索，同時左手穩穩接住溜溜，把牠像接棒球一樣，捧在掌心上。\n\n溜溜趴在高老師手心裡，四腳朝天，尾巴僵直，電子眼裡一片空白。\n\n「溜溜，」高老師低頭，看著掌心的小寵物，「依照校規，考試期間傳遞答案，屬嚴重違規。雖然你是全班合養的寵物，但這筆帳，我先記在你的『行為觀察記錄簿』上。」\n\n他從口袋裡掏出一個小本子，翻到寫著「溜溜」的那一頁，用鋼筆工工整整地畫下一個大大的「叉」。\n\n溜溜的尾巴，像斷了電一樣，軟軟地垂了下去。\n\n「嗚……嗶……」溜溜發出委屈的電子音，阿釁心疼得眼眶都紅了。\n\n「啪！」\n\n教室門又一次被推開，周嚴主任大步流星地闖進來，興奮地揚著登記簿：「我剛剛在走廊聽到『咻咻咻』的聲音！一定是你們在——」\n\n他話說一半，看到滿地的紙飛機、彈到牆角的橡皮筋，以及高老師手裡那條掛著粉筆盒的吊索，整個人愣住了。\n\n「呃……你們在幹嘛？」\n\n「周主任，」高老師面色平靜地舉起那架被夾住的紙飛機，「本班正在進行『飛行原理』實驗課。這架紙飛機，是尪同学設計的『升力模型』；這條橡皮筋，是巫同学研發的『彈射發射器』；而這個粉筆盒吊艙，是我們班『溜溜航空』的空投實驗。教育部最新課綱，鼓勵跨領域動手做。」\n\n「飛、飛行原理？」周嚴瞪大眼睛，左看看右看看，最後狐疑地掃了一圈，「那為什麼紙飛機上……好像有字？」\n\n「那是『設計標註』。」高老師面不改色，「記錄實驗數據用的。」\n\n「……」周嚴張了張嘴，實在找不到破綻，最後只能悻悻地合上登記簿，「哼……動手做是吧？做得好，就幫你們班報名全市科展！」\n\n「真的嗎！」阿釁的眼睛瞬間亮了。\n\n周嚴走後，全班虛脫地癱在椅子上。\n\n高老師把那堆紙飛機、橡皮筋、粉筆盒吊艙，全部整整齊齊地收進一個紙箱，擺到講台角落：\n\n「各位同學，這些『實驗器材』，我先保管了。明天開始，我們正式進入月考衝刺——希望大家把剛才『飛』的力氣，用在『讀』上面。」\n\n他頓了頓，補了一句：「順帶一提，剛才那場模擬考，全班的平均分數，比上周進步了十二分。」\n\n全班鴉雀無聲。\n\n「進步十二分？！」阿釁難以置信地瞪大眼睛，「怎麼可能？我們都在傳答案啊！」\n\n「因為你們在準備『傳答案』的過程中，」晴晴推了推眼鏡，語氣平靜，「把該複習的重點，全部又看了一遍。」\n\n阿釁愣住了。\n\n他看了看講台上那箱被沒收的「實驗器材」，又看了看自己那張寫得滿滿的模擬考卷——明明整場考試都在忙著指揮傳遞，他卻發現，自己好像……每一題都會寫？\n\n「奇怪……」阿釁喃喃自語，「我怎麼覺得……我好像也不需要傳答案？」\n\n「阿釁，」老巫湊過來，小聲問，「那……我們還作弊嗎？」\n\n阿釁沉默了三秒。\n\n然後，他「啪」地一拍桌子，站起身，眼中燃起新的鬥志：\n\n「作！當然作！三路全滅不算什麼！我宣布——第三號計畫，暗號大作戰！」\n\n窗外的溜溜，趴在高老師的「行為觀察記錄簿」上，無力地甩了甩尾巴，發出一聲悠長的電子嘆息：\n\n「嗶……人類的固執，果然沒有極限……」","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 3: Paper Planes and Rubber Band Conveyor Belt\n\n\"Everyone! The Miniature Library has fallen!\"\n\nIn the classroom after school, A-Xin snapped a piece of chalk in two and slapped it on the podium in righteous indignation:\n\n\"But failure doesn't mean the end! Teacher Gao has X-ray vision, so we just—don't hide anything anymore! We'll go with 'transporting'!\"\n\n\"Transporting? Transport what?\" Old Wu asked through a mouthful of pork bun.\n\n\"Transport—the answers!\" A-Xin drew three big characters on the blackboard. \"Plan No. 2: The Aerial Delivery System!\"\n\nHe unrolled a design drawing full of scribbles, covered with dense arrows, dashed lines, and mysterious circles:\n\n\"Everyone, take a look! Instead of having everyone risk being scanned to hide cheat sheets, let's have the smartest person among us 'know the answers,' and then—air-drop them to everyone!\"\n\n\"So we need a 'main unit'?\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses.\n\n\"Yes! And the main unit is—\" A-Xin's gaze swept the class and finally landed on the girl in the front row who was busy doing homework, \"Weixi!\"\n\nLin Weixi raised her head, a hint of confusion in her eyes: \"Me?\"\n\n\"Your grades are the best!\" A-Xin leaned in, palms pressed together. \"Weixi, if you'll just transmit the answers to everyone during the mock exam, the whole class is saved!\"\n\n\"I don't cheat.\" Weixi's answer was clean and crisp.\n\n\"But...\"\n\n\"And besides,\" Weixi shook her head gently, \"A-Xin, answers delivered by 'passing' will always be passed wrong, passed short, or passed slow someday. The only truly reliable answers are the ones already in your own head.\"\n\n\"That's because your head is good!\" A-Xin clutched his own head and wailed.\n\n\"Then—make everyone's heads good too.\" Weixi left those gentle words and went back to her homework.\n\n\"Fine! If you won't be the main unit, we'll build our own!\" A-Xin turned to the class, pointing at the design drawing. \"Airdrop system, three routes in parallel! Route one—paper planes! Route two—rubber band slingshot! Route three—chalk box airdrop, piloted by Liu-Liu in person!\"\n\n\"Beep?\" Liu-Liu poked its head out of the ventilation duct, its electronic eyes plainly saying \"What's it got to do with me?\"\n\n\"Liu-Liu! The whole class is entrusting you with a great responsibility!\" A-Xin pulled out a can of lubricating oil and waved it in front of Liu-Liu. \"Mission accomplished, and this can of 'top-grade space lubricant' is yours!\"\n\nLiu-Liu's electronic eyes instantly blazed like two little suns, its tail standing straight up, letting out an excited electronic chirp:\n\n\"Beep beep beep! Roger! Liu-Liu Airlines, ready for takeoff!\"\n\n\"Good! Everyone, get to work!\"\n\nAnd so, the underground factory of the Exam Mutual Aid Society started production in full swing.\n\nWang Zhuankai was in charge of folding paper planes. He folded a dozen in a row, every one crooked, some with wings of mismatched lengths, some with noses flattened as if they'd been stepped on. A-Xin stared at them for a long while before he couldn't help complaining:\n\n\"Your planes... can they even fly?\"\n\n\"Whether they fly or not is one thing,\" Wang Zhuankai said with full confidence, \"the point is—they're cool!\"\n\n\"Cool? This is 'cool'? I'd call it 'drool'!\" A-Xin held his forehead helplessly.\n\nOver on the other side, Old Wu was frowning at a thick rubber band. He slipped it over his fingers, pulled it hard—\"whoosh\"—the rubber band shot out and hit a paper plane dead-on, snapping its nose in two.\n\n\"Wow! Old Wu! Are you testing force or destruction?\" A-Xin jumped up and yelled.\n\n\"I-I'm just testing the strength!\" Old Wu rubbed his fingers aggrievedly. \"Who knew it would be this powerful...\"\n\n\"You used the plane I folded myself to test it!\" Wang Zhuankai cradled the wreckage lovingly.\n\nIn the corner, Qingqing was silently assembling the third route—the chalk box airdrop pod. She disassembled three chalk boxes, taped them into a simple hanging gondola, strapped Liu-Liu's special harness in the middle, and fixed two balance wings cut from rulers on the front and back.\n\n\"Airdrop pod complete.\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses. \"In theory, Liu-Liu takes off carrying the answer sheet, flies to the target's airspace, releases the pod, and the answer sheet lands precisely at the designated spot. Estimated margin of error: within three centimeters.\"\n\n\"A three-centimeter error?\" A-Xin widened his eyes. \"That's basically the distance of 'dropping onto Old Wu's pork bun'!\"\n\n\"Precisely.\" Qingqing nodded calmly. \"Which is why I've set the target as—the center of Old Wu's desk.\"\n\n\"Why me?\" Old Wu screamed.\n\n\"Because you're Customer No. 1.\" Qingqing didn't even look up.\n\nThe next day, the school-wide mock exam before the monthly exam, right on schedule.\n\nAs the test papers were handed out, A-Xin sat in the first row as the \"answer relay station\"; Old Wu sat in the fifth row as \"Customer No. 1\"; outside the window, Liu-Liu, clutching a paper full of answers, was already in position on the eave.\n\n\"Everyone!\" A-Xin recited silently in his head. \"Everything hinges on this! With three routes of airdrops, at least one has to succeed!\"\n\n\"Chirp—\"\n\nRoute one, the paper plane, took off.\n\nWang Zhuankai tossed his painstakingly folded \"cool fighter\" diagonally backward. The paper plane, dragging a crooked arc, wobbled toward Old Wu—\n\n\"Slap.\"\n\nTwo fingers caught the paper plane's wing midair, steady as can be.\n\nTeacher Gao Zhixian stood on the podium, a golden ring appearing in his pupils behind his lenses, his tone as flat as a weather report:\n\n\"Wang Zhuankai, the flight parameters of this paper plane of yours: initial velocity two point one meters per second, elevation angle thirty-one degrees, affected by the airflow from the desk fan on the podium, it would have drifted forty-five degrees off target. Incidentally—even if it had landed successfully, the writing on it isn't the answer you wanted.\"\n\nThe whole class gasped.\n\n\"Three-dimensional trajectory tracking system activated.\" Teacher Gao pushed up his glasses. \"Everyone, please don't test your teacher's computational abilities.\"\n\nA-Xin gritted his teeth: \"Never mind! There's still route two!\"\n\nOld Wu, trembling, slipped the rubber band over his fingers, aimed at A-Xin's direction, and pulled hard—\"whoosh\"—the rubber band, carrying a square of folded answer paper, whistled out!\n\n\"Slap!\"\n\nCaught again.\n\nWithout even turning his head, Teacher Gao casually raised his hand and precisely intercepted the paper between his fingers, while the rubber band snapped back and \"slapped\" Old Wu right on his own forehead, leaving a red mark.\n\n\"Mr. Wu,\" Teacher Gao let out a sigh, \"this rubber band of yours has an elasticity modulus of zero point eight and a rebound rate of ninety-three percent. Your chances of hitting yourself are six times higher than your chances of hitting me.\"\n\n\"Ow...\" Old Wu held his forehead, eyes brimming with tears.\n\n\"There's still the last route!\" A-Xin steeled himself and gave the signal. \"Liu-Liu! Go!\"\n\nOutside the window, Liu-Liu, clutching the chalk box pod full of answer papers, swooped down from the eave like a silver-white little rocket! Its ears pressed flat, its tail carving a graceful arc through the air, aiming straight for Old Wu's desk—\n\n\"Liu-Liu Airlines, final sprint!\"\n\n\"Whoosh—!\"\n\nJust as the pod was about to reach its target, Teacher Gao's right hand shot out at a speed that defied human ergonomics, grabbed the pod's suspension line midair, and with his left hand caught Liu-Liu, holding it up in his palm like a caught baseball.\n\nLiu-Liu lay in Teacher Gao's palm, four paws in the air, tail rigid, electronic eyes blank.\n\n\"Liu-Liu,\" Teacher Gao looked down at the little pet in his hand, \"according to school rules, passing answers during an exam is a serious violation. Although you're the class's collective pet, I'll still record this on your 'behavior observation log' first.\"\n\nHe pulled a small notebook from his pocket, flipped to the page labeled \"Liu-Liu,\" and meticulously drew a big \"X\" with his pen.\n\nLiu-Liu's tail drooped limply, as if its power had been cut off.\n\n\"Ow... beep...\" Liu-Liu let out a pitiful electronic whimper, and A-Xin's eyes reddened with heartache.\n\n\"Slap!\"\n\nThe classroom door was pushed open again, and Director Zhou Yan barged in triumphantly, waving his notebook: \"I heard 'whoosh whoosh whoosh' sounds from the hallway! You must be—\"\n\nHe stopped mid-sentence, seeing the paper planes all over the floor, the rubber band that had snapped into the corner of the wall, and the chalk box pod hanging from Teacher Gao's hand. He froze.\n\n\"Uh... what are you doing?\"\n\n\"Director Zhou,\" Teacher Gao said calmly, holding up the intercepted paper plane, \"our class is conducting a 'flight principles' experiment class. This paper plane is Wang's 'lift model'; this rubber band is Wu's 'catapult launcher'; and this chalk box pod is our class's 'Liu-Liu Airlines' airdrop experiment. The latest Ministry of Education curriculum encourages cross-disciplinary hands-on learning.\"\n\n\"Fl-Flight principles?\" Director Zhou stared wide-eyed, glancing left and right, and finally scanned the room suspiciously. \"Then why does the paper plane... seem to have writing on it?\"\n\n\"That's the 'design annotation.'\" Teacher Gao said without changing his expression. \"For recording the experimental data.\"\n\n\"...\" Director Zhou opened his mouth, unable to find any flaw. In the end, he grudgingly snapped his notebook shut. \"Hmph... hands-on learning, huh? If you do it well, I'll sign you up for the city-wide science fair!\"\n\n\"Really?!\" A-Xin's eyes lit up instantly.\n\nAfter Director Zhou left, the whole class collapsed limply into their chairs.\n\nTeacher Gao collected all the paper planes, rubber bands, and chalk box pods neatly into a cardboard box and set it at the corner of the podium:\n\n\"Everyone, I'll keep these 'experimental apparatus' safe for now. Starting tomorrow, we formally enter the monthly exam sprint—I hope everyone will put the energy they used 'flying' just now into 'studying.'\"\n\nHe paused, then added: \"Incidentally, in that mock exam just now, the class average improved by twelve points compared to last week.\"\n\nThe whole class was dead silent.\n\n\"Up twelve points?!\" A-Xin couldn't believe it. \"How is that possible? We were all busy passing answers!\"\n\n\"Because in the process of preparing to 'pass answers,'\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses, her tone calm, \"you went through all the review key points again.\"\n\nA-Xin froze.\n\nHe looked at the box of confiscated \"experimental apparatus\" on the podium, then at his own mock exam paper, filled with writing—he'd spent the whole exam directing the deliveries, and yet he realized... he seemed to know how to answer every question?\n\n\"Strange...\" A-Xin murmured to himself. \"Why do I feel like... I didn't even need to pass answers?\"\n\n\"A-Xin,\" Old Wu leaned over and asked quietly, \"so... do we still cheat?\"\n\nA-Xin was silent for three seconds.\n\nThen, he \"slapped\" the table and stood up, fresh fighting spirit blazing in his eyes:\n\n\"Cheat! Of course we cheat! Three routes wiped out is nothing! I declare—Plan No. 3, the Code Signaling Operation!\"\n\nOutside the window, Liu-Liu lay sprawled on Teacher Gao's \"behavior observation log,\" wearily flicking its tail and letting out a long electronic sigh:\n\n\"Beep... human stubbornness really has no limits...\""},{"id":4,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第四章：咳嗽密碼與摩斯手勢\n\n「各位！紙飛機陣亡、橡皮筋陣亡、溜溜航空也陣亡了！」\n\n放學後的教室裡，阿釁站在課桌上，兩手叉腰，氣勢磅礡：\n\n「但是！我剛剛發現一個最重要的關鍵——前三場戰鬥，我們都輸在『身上帶著東西』！只要帶著東西，就會被掃描！」\n\n「所以咧？」老巫啃著肉包，含糊地問。\n\n「所以這次！」阿釁「啪」地一拍手，「我們什麼都不帶！用『信號』！」\n\n他轉身，在黑板上畫出密密麻麻的符號：\n\n「第三號計畫：暗號大作戰！規則如下——」\n\n「摸左耳，答案A！」\n「摸右耳，答案B！」\n「摸鼻子，答案C！」\n「摸下巴，答案D！」\n「咳嗽幾聲，就是第幾題！」\n\n「也就是說——」阿釁興奮地比劃，「你咳嗽兩聲，就是告訴大家：第二題要出動了！然後你再摸一下左耳，大家就知道：第二題答案是A！」\n\n「哇——！」老巫眼睛瞪得溜圓，「這、這不是武俠片的暗號嗎！」\n\n「那是當然！」阿釁得意洋洋，「這次沒帶任何紙條，高老師就算掃描一千遍，也掃不到東西！因為答案，就藏在你我之間！」\n\n「從資訊理論的角度來說……」晴晴推了推眼鏡，「這個系統有一個致命缺陷。」\n\n「什麼缺陷？」阿釁問。\n\n「咳嗽是聽覺信號，摸耳是視覺信號。」晴晴平靜地分析，「兩種信號，都需要『傳遞者』和『接收者』同時注意。只要有一個人漏看、漏聽，整串信息就會斷掉。」\n\n「所以我們要訓練！」阿釁大手一揮，「全員！開始排練！」\n\n於是，一場荒謬絕倫的「暗號特訓」，在六年一班的地下教室如火如荼地展開了。\n\n「咳！」\n\n阿釁清了一下喉嚨，然後摸了一下左耳。\n\n「第二題……不，等一下！」老巫慌慌張張地站起來，「阿釁，你咳嗽一聲，到底是第一題，還是第二題？」\n\n「咳嗽一聲，就是第一題啊！」阿釁無奈地嘆氣，「老巫，你的記性被肉包塞住了嗎？」\n\n「可是我剛剛明明聽到你咳了兩聲啊！」老巫委屈。\n\n「那一聲是我真的在清喉嚨！不是暗號！」阿釁暴跳如雷。\n\n「那、那怎麼分得出來嘛！」老巫哀嚎。\n\n「咳跟『咳』，節奏不一樣！」阿釁示範，「暗號咳嗽要短促有力——『咳』！一般咳嗽是拖長音的——『咳咳咳』……」\n\n他話還沒說完，尪伝恺就真的打了一個超大的噴嚏：\n\n「哈——啾！」\n\n全班「唰」地一聲，同時摸向自己的左耳、右耳、鼻子、下巴，亂成一團。\n\n「誰打噴嚏！誰！重傷！」阿釁氣得跳腳，「打噴嚏不算暗號！不準在考場打噴嚏！」\n\n「我、我忍不住啊！」尪伝恺揉著鼻子，委屈地辯解。\n\n晴晴默默地在角落寫了一張紙，遞給阿釁：\n\n「建議：建立『訊號過濾系統』。所有動作，必須重複兩次才算數。例如摸耳朵兩次，才代表答案B。」\n\n「重複兩次？」阿釁沉吟，「這樣不是更慢嗎？」\n\n「但至少不會被噴嚏、咳嗽、眨眼干擾。」晴晴說，「情報的正確性，比速度重要。」\n\n「好！就依妳的！」阿釁拍板，「全員記住！以後所有暗號，一律重複兩次！」\n\n月考前一週，第三次模擬考，準時登場。\n\n阿釁坐在最後一排，負責當「總機」；老巫坐在第一排，負責接收。為了避免露餡，全班二十五人（未晞不參加），全部戴上了口罩。\n\n考卷發下來。\n\n第一題。阿釁在心裡默數：「一！」他清了一下喉嚨：「咳——咳——」\n\n然後，他迅速地摸了兩下左耳。\n\n老巫屏住呼吸，在心裡翻譯：「咳嗽兩聲＝第二題……摸兩次左耳＝答案A！」\n\n他正要低頭填答案——\n\n「巫茞輆同學。」\n\n高峙舷老師的聲音，從講台上傳了下來，語氣平淡得像在報告天氣：\n\n「剛才，你總共眨了三次眼，摸了摸兩次耳朵，視線在阿釁同學的位置停留了六秒鐘。根據『語音波形分析』，你剛剛接收到的那組信號，翻譯成暗號是——第二題，答案A，對嗎？」\n\n全班的口罩底下，二十六張臉全部僵住。\n\n高老師走下講台，走到阿釁面前，鏡片後的瞳孔浮現一圈金色的光圈：\n\n「轆慄釁同學，你剛才咳嗽的波形：頻率四百二十赫茲，持續時間零點三秒，聲壓八十五分貝。這個波形，和你練習暗號時的咳嗽，一模一樣。」\n\n他從口袋裡掏出一支筆，在黑板上畫出一道波形曲線：\n\n「各位同學，這就是『暗號識別系統』。咳嗽的聲波，摸耳的動作，鼻子的角度，下巴的弧度——所有信號，都會被記錄、比對、還原。」\n\n「那、那我們……」阿釁的聲音開始發抖。\n\n「還原結果如下。」高老師在黑板上，一筆一劃寫下：\n\n```\n摸左耳×2 ＝ 答案 A\n摸右耳×2 ＝ 答案 B\n摸鼻子×2 ＝ 答案 C\n摸下巴×2 ＝ 答案 D\n咳嗽 N 聲 ＝ 第 N 題\n```\n\n全班看到黑板上的「暗號對照表」，集體倒抽一口涼氣。\n\n老巫嚇得直接把口罩拉起來遮住整張臉，聲音從口罩裡悶悶地傳出來：「老、老師，你是怎麼知道我們用這個的？」\n\n「因為……」高老師放下粉筆，語氣真誠，「你們練習暗號的時候，我正好路過，聽到了完整的『情報』。」\n\n「——！」阿釁整個人僵在原地，臉上的表情像是被雷劈中了一樣。\n\n他萬萬沒想到，自己辛苦設計的暗號系統，竟然在練習的當天，就被高老師完整錄音了！\n\n「還有，」高老師補了一刀，「你們戴著口罩咳嗽，聲波會被布料過濾，音頻更清晰——這在聲學上，叫做『濾波器』。下次要打暗號，建議不要戴口罩。」\n\n「嗚……」阿釁頹然地癱在椅子上。\n\n「砰！」\n\n教室門又被推開，周嚴主任大步衝了進來，臉色緊張：\n\n「怎麼回事！我剛才聽到教室裡『咳咳咳』咳個不停！是不是流感爆發了！」\n\n他環顧四周，看到全班二十六人（包括未晞）都戴著口罩，臉色瞬間刷白：「都、都戴口罩了？！」\n\n「周主任，」高老師面色平靜，「本班正在進行『國語朗讀發音訓練』。咳嗽，是練習聲母『ㄎ』的發聲技巧。」\n\n「練、練習聲母？」周嚴瞪大眼睛，看看高老師，又看看那群戴著口罩、眼神躲閃的學生，「ㄎ？！」\n\n「請聽，」高老師示範，「ㄎ——ㄎ——這是『課』字的聲母。學生們正在集體發音。」\n\n全班默契地齊聲：「ㄎ——！ㄎ——！」\n\n周嚴嘴角抽搐，看了看手上的登記簿，最後還是悻悻然地退了出來：「……神經病啊你們！」\n\n周嚴走後，高老師把黑板上的「暗號對照表」擦掉，重新寫上幾個大字：\n\n「各位，暗號系統雖然失敗了，但它其實很有價值——因為它證明了，你們已經學會『分類整理』。」\n\n他指著黑板：「摸左耳是A、摸右耳是B……這其實就是『把選項分類』的記憶法。與其用暗號傳遞答案，不如把這套分類法，用在整理重點上。」\n\n「老師……」老巫舉手，「那這套暗號表，還有用嗎？」\n\n「有。」高老師微微一笑，把一張印好的「重點分類記憶卡」發給全班，「從今天起，這就是我們的複習口訣。摸左耳，記住A的答案；摸右耳，記住B的答案。考試的時候，你只要摸摸自己的耳朵，就能想起答案。」\n\n「摸自己的耳朵……」老巫半信半疑地摸了摸自己的左耳，「咦？這樣真的想得起來嗎？」\n\n「重點是『記』，不是『摸』。」高老師說。\n\n放學後，考試互助會的緊急會議，氣氛凝重得像喪禮。\n\n「各位……」阿釁雙手抱頭，痛苦地趴在桌上，「我們輸了……徹底輸了……我們的三套作戰計畫，全部陣亡了……」\n\n「阿釁，」晴晴開口，「你有沒有發現一件事？我們每次準備作弊，成績反而都會變好？」\n\n「那只是巧合！」阿釁跳起來，「巧合！你懂嗎！」\n\n「那這次呢？」晴晴問，「這次我們的模擬考，你覺得你能考及格嗎？」\n\n阿釁張了張嘴，卻發現自己竟然……答不出來。\n\n他回想了一下，剛才那場模擬考，雖然整場都在忙著指揮暗號，但那些題目，他好像全都……看得懂？\n\n「這、這不對啊！」阿釁抓著頭髮，「我明明都在想暗號，怎麼會看得懂題目？」\n\n「因為你想暗號的時候，」晴晴平靜地補刀，「把題目也一起看進去了。」\n\n「……」阿釁沉默了整整十秒。\n\n然後，他猛地站起來，握緊拳頭，眼中燃起熊熊鬥志：\n\n「既然人力作弊會被抓，那我們就用——科技！第四號計畫：作弊科技革命，正式啟動！」\n\n「可是阿釁……」老巫弱弱地舉手，「月考……後天就要到了耶。」\n\n阿釁的動作瞬間定格。\n\n他僵硬地轉頭，看了看牆上的月曆——後天，就是月考！\n\n「……科技的事，先放一邊。」阿釁深吸一口氣，語氣突然變得莊嚴，「既然時間來不及了，我們只能動用——最後的殺手鐧！」\n\n「什麼殺手鐧？」老巫緊張地問。\n\n阿釁神秘一笑，湊近全班，壓低聲音：\n\n「人體拼圖。二十六人，一人記一塊。月考當天，拼出完整答案！」","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 4: Cough Codes and Morse Gestures\n\n\"Everyone! Paper planes are down, rubber bands are down, and Liu-Liu Airlines is down too!\"\n\nIn the classroom after school, A-Xin stood on his desk, hands on his hips, radiating momentum:\n\n\"But just now I realized the most important thing—in the first three battles, we all lost because we were 'carrying things'! As long as you carry something, it can be scanned!\"\n\n\"So?\" Old Wu chewed his pork bun vaguely.\n\n\"So this time!\" A-Xin \"slapped\" his palms together. \"We don't carry anything! We use 'signals'!\"\n\nHe turned and drew a dense jumble of symbols on the blackboard:\n\n\"Plan No. 3: The Code Signaling Operation! Rules as follows—\"\n\n\"Touch your left ear, answer A!\"\n\"Touch your right ear, answer B!\"\n\"Touch your nose, answer C!\"\n\"Touch your chin, answer D!\"\n\"Cough N times, that's question N!\"\n\n\"Which means—\" A-Xin gestured excitedly, \"you cough twice, telling everyone: question two is in play! Then you touch your left ear once, and everyone knows: the answer to question two is A!\"\n\n\"Wow—!\" Old Wu's eyes went wide as saucers. \"Isn't this like kung-fu movie codes?!\"\n\n\"Of course!\" A-Xin said smugly. \"This time we're carrying no paper at all. No matter how many times Teacher Gao scans, he can't find anything! Because the answers are hidden between us!\"\n\n\"From an information-theory standpoint...\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses, \"this system has one fatal flaw.\"\n\n\"What flaw?\" A-Xin asked.\n\n\"Coughing is an auditory signal; touching your ear is a visual signal.\" Qingqing analyzed calmly. \"Both signals require the 'transmitter' and the 'receiver' to pay attention at the same time. If a single person misses a look or a sound, the whole message chain breaks.\"\n\n\"So we train!\" A-Xin waved his arm. \"Everyone! Begin rehearsal!\"\n\nAnd so, an absurd \"code-signal drill\" unfolded in full swing in Class 6-1's underground classroom.\n\n\"Cough!\"\n\nA-Xin cleared his throat, then touched his left ear.\n\n\"Question two... no, wait!\" Old Wu jumped up in a panic. \"A-Xin, you coughed once. Is that question one, or question two?\"\n\n\"Coughing once means question one!\" A-Xin sighed helplessly. \"Old Wu, has your memory been stuffed with pork buns?\"\n\n\"But I just heard you cough twice!\" Old Wu said aggrievedly.\n\n\"That cough was me clearing my throat for real! Not a code!\" A-Xin stamped his foot.\n\n\"Then... then how are we supposed to tell the difference?\" Old Wu wailed.\n\n\"A real cough and a code cough have different rhythms!\" A-Xin demonstrated. \"A code cough has to be short and forceful—'cough'! A real cough drags—'cough-cough-cough'...\"\n\nBefore he could finish, Wang Zhuankai sneezed for real:\n\n\"Hah—choo!\"\n\nThe whole class \"snapped\" simultaneously to touch their left ears, right ears, noses, and chins, turning into total chaos.\n\n\"Who sneezed! Who! Serious injury!\" A-Xin hopped in fury. \"A sneeze doesn't count as a code! No sneezing in the exam room!\"\n\n\"I-I can't help it!\" Wang Zhuankai rubbed his nose aggrievedly.\n\nQingqing quietly wrote a note in the corner and handed it to A-Xin:\n\n\"Recommendation: establish a 'signal filter system.' Every action must be repeated twice to count. For example, touching your ear twice means answer B.\"\n\n\"Repeated twice?\" A-Xin pondered. \"Doesn't that make it slower?\"\n\n\"But at least it won't be disturbed by sneezes, coughs, or blinks.\" Qingqing said. \"Accuracy matters more than speed.\"\n\n\"Fine! We'll do it your way!\" A-Xin made the call. \"Everyone, remember! From now on, every code has to be repeated twice!\"\n\nOne week before the monthly exam, the third mock exam arrived on schedule.\n\nA-Xin sat in the last row as the \"switchboard\"; Old Wu sat in the first row as the receiver. To avoid exposure, all twenty-five of them (Weixi wasn't participating) wore masks.\n\nThe test paper was handed out.\n\nQuestion one. A-Xin counted silently in his head: \"One!\" He cleared his throat: \"Cough—cough—\"\n\nThen, he quickly touched his left ear twice.\n\nOld Wu held his breath, translating in his head: \"Coughing twice = question two... touching the left ear twice = answer A!\"\n\nHe was just about to lower his head and fill in the answer—\n\n\"Wu Chenkai.\"\n\nTeacher Gao Zhixian's voice came down from the podium, flat as a weather report:\n\n\"Just now, you blinked three times total, touched your ear twice, and your gaze lingered on A-Xin's seat for six seconds. According to voice waveform analysis, the signal you just received, translated, is—question two, answer A. Correct?\"\n\nTwenty-six faces, all under masks, froze at once.\n\nTeacher Gao stepped off the podium and walked to A-Xin, a golden ring in his pupils behind his lenses:\n\n\"Lu Lixin, the waveform of your cough just now: frequency four hundred and twenty hertz, duration zero point three seconds, sound pressure eighty-five decibels. This waveform is exactly the same as the cough you used while practicing codes.\"\n\nHe pulled a pen from his pocket and drew a waveform curve on the blackboard:\n\n\"Everyone, this is the 'code recognition system.' The sound waves of coughs, the motion of ear-touching, the angle of noses, the curve of chins—every signal gets recorded, compared, and decoded.\"\n\n\"So we...\" A-Xin's voice began to tremble.\n\n\"Decoding result as follows.\" Teacher Gao wrote on the blackboard, stroke by stroke:\n\n```\nTouch left ear x2 = Answer A\nTouch right ear x2 = Answer B\nTouch nose x2 = Answer C\nTouch chin x2 = Answer D\nCough N times = Question N\n```\n\nThe whole class, seeing the \"code comparison table\" on the blackboard, gasped collectively.\n\nOld Wu was so startled he pulled his mask up over his whole face, his voice muffled: \"T-Teacher, how did you know we were using this?\"\n\n\"Because,\" Teacher Gao put down the chalk, his tone sincere, \"when you were rehearsing the codes, I happened to pass by and heard the complete 'intelligence.'\"\n\n\"—!\" A-Xin stood frozen on the spot, his expression as if he'd been struck by lightning.\n\nHe never imagined that the code system he'd painstakingly designed had been fully recorded by Teacher Gao the very day of the rehearsal!\n\n\"Also,\" Teacher Gao added the finishing blow, \"when you cough while wearing masks, the sound waves get filtered by the fabric, making the audio even clearer—in acoustics, this is called a 'filter.' Next time you want to send codes, I suggest not wearing masks.\"\n\n\"Ow...\" A-Xin slumped limply into his chair.\n\n\"Bang!\"\n\nThe classroom door was pushed open again, and Director Zhou Yan rushed in, his face tense:\n\n\"What's going on! I heard 'cough cough cough' coming from the classroom! Has the flu broken out?!\"\n\nHe scanned the room, saw all twenty-six of them (including Weixi) wearing masks, and his face instantly went white: \"Everyone... has masks?!\"\n\n\"Director Zhou,\" Teacher Gao said calmly, \"our class is currently conducting 'Chinese recitation vocal training.' The coughing is the practice of pronouncing the consonant 'k'.\"\n\n\"P-Pronouncing the consonant?\" Director Zhou stared wide-eyed at Teacher Gao, then at the group of students with masks and evasive eyes. \"'K'?!\"\n\n\"Please listen,\" Teacher Gao demonstrated, \"k—k—this is the initial consonant of the word 'ke' (lesson). The students are doing a collective vocal exercise.\"\n\nThe whole class, in perfect unison, chanted: \"K—! K—!\"\n\nDirector Zhou's mouth twitched. He looked at his notebook, and in the end, he shuffled out grumbling: \"...You people are crazy!\"\n\nAfter Director Zhou left, Teacher Gao erased the \"code comparison table\" from the blackboard and wrote a few large words in its place:\n\n\"Everyone, the code system failed, but it actually has value—because it proves you've learned 'classification and organization.'\"\n\nHe pointed at the blackboard: \"Touch left ear for A, touch right ear for B... this is actually a memory method of 'classifying options.' Instead of using codes to pass answers, why not use this classification method to organize your review points?\"\n\n\"Teacher,\" Old Wu raised his hand, \"so this code table... is it still useful?\"\n\n\"It is.\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly, handing each student a printed \"key-point classification memory card.\" \"Starting today, this is our review mnemonic. Touch your left ear to remember the answer to A; touch your right ear to remember the answer to B. On the exam, just touch your own ear, and you'll recall the answer.\"\n\n\"Touch my own ear...\" Old Wu half-believing, half-doubting, touched his left ear. \"Huh? Can I actually recall it this way?\"\n\n\"The key is 'remembering,' not 'touching.'\" Teacher Gao said.\n\nAfter school, the emergency meeting of the Exam Mutual Aid Society was as heavy as a funeral.\n\n\"Everyone...\" A-Xin clutched his head, groaning in pain, slumped over his desk. \"We lost... completely lost... all three of our battle plans are dead...\"\n\n\"A-Xin,\" Qingqing spoke, \"have you noticed something? Every time we prepare to cheat, our grades improve anyway?\"\n\n\"That's just a coincidence!\" A-Xin jumped up. \"A coincidence! You understand?\"\n\n\"Then what about this time?\" Qingqing asked. \"In this mock exam, do you think you passed?\"\n\nA-Xin opened his mouth, but found he couldn't answer at all.\n\nHe thought back. In that mock exam, although he'd spent the whole time directing the codes, those questions... he seemed to understand all of them?\n\n\"Th-This isn't right!\" A-Xin grabbed his hair. \"I was thinking about codes the whole time, so how could I understand the questions?\"\n\n\"Because while you were thinking about codes,\" Qingqing delivered the finishing blow calmly, \"you read the questions too.\"\n\n\"...\" A-Xin was silent for a full ten seconds.\n\nThen, he abruptly stood up, clenched his fists, fighting spirit blazing in his eyes:\n\n\"Since human cheating gets caught, we'll use—technology! Plan No. 4: The Cheating Technology Revolution, officially launched!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin...\" Old Wu weakly raised his hand. \"The monthly exam... is in two days.\"\n\nA-Xin's movements froze.\n\nHe stiffly turned his head and looked at the calendar on the wall—in two days, the monthly exam!\n\n\"...Let's set technology aside for now.\" A-Xin took a deep breath, his tone suddenly solemn. \"Since there's no time, we'll have to use the final trump card!\"\n\n\"What trump card?\" Old Wu asked nervously.\n\nA-Xin smiled mysteriously, leaning in close to the class, his voice low:\n\n\"The human puzzle. Twenty-six people, each memorizing one piece. On exam day, we piece together the complete answer!\""},{"id":5,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第五章：二十六人的完美分工\n\n月考當天，天空陰得像一塊泡過水的抹布。\n\n六年一班的教室裡，二十六張課桌被拉成標準的單人單座考場，桌面上的書本雜物清得一乾二淨，只有鉛筆盒、墊板和一把直尺。\n\n阿釁坐在最後一排，趁著高老師低頭整理考卷的空檔，用氣音對前排的老巫下達最後指令：\n\n「老巫！你負責的是自然科的『氣體交換』單元，記住了嗎！」\n\n「記住了！」老巫緊張地點頭，「氣體交換……氣體交換……我連做夢都在交換氣體！」\n\n「還有，你那一科總共負責六題，記住，六題！其餘的全部空著，等著抄我們的！」\n\n「可是阿釁……」老巫顫抖地問，「如果高老師不給我們抄，怎麼辦？」\n\n「他會給我們抄的！」阿釁斬釘截鐵，「因為我們有『縫隙戰術』！他總有轉頭的時候！」\n\n「各位同學，」高峙舷老師的聲音從講台上響起，「月考正式開始前，請容我提醒——」\n\n他頓了頓，推了推黑框眼鏡：\n\n「根據教育部考場規定，監考老師必須全程注視考生，以維護考試公平。所以今天，我會站在這裡，從考試開始到結束，一秒都不會轉頭。」\n\n「一秒都不轉頭？！」阿釁的心「咯噔」一聲往下沉。\n\n「是的。」高老師站定，雙手負在身後，像一尊雕像，目光如同兩道雷射光束，掃射著全班，「請各位安心作答。」\n\n考試開始。\n\n阿釁在心中默數：「等一下他一定會眨眼、一定會擦眼鏡、一定會看窗外——只要有一秒縫隙，我們就出手！」\n\n他等了整整十分鐘。\n\n高老師像一台被釘在講台上的監視器，眼睛連眨都沒眨一下。\n\n「怎麼可能……」阿釁額頭冒汗，「人類怎麼可能連眨眼都不用？！」\n\n他決定主動製造縫隙。\n\n「啪嗒！」阿釁用力把鉛筆盒推到地上，發出巨響，「哎呀！老師！我鉛筆盒掉了！」\n\n「嗯。」高老師的目光，連動都沒動，「請撿起來，繼續作答。」\n\n「我、我順便擦一下眼淚！」阿釁蹲下去，偷偷朝老巫的方向比了一個「準備行動」的手勢。\n\n高老師的目光，像黏在阿釁身上一樣，紋絲不動。\n\n「老師！窗戶外面有鳥！」尪伝恺突然大喊。\n\n「窗外的鳥，」高老師頭也不回，「是灰面鵟鷹，遷徙季節，從南方飛來。請繼續作答。」\n\n「老師！天花板在滴水！」林芸芸尖叫。\n\n「那是冷凝水，」高老師平靜地回應，「由於教室相對濕度較高，冷氣出風口凝結的水珠。請繼續作答。」\n\n阿釁徹底絕望了。\n\n這個老師……根本就是一堵人形牆壁！不管他製造多少縫隙，高老師都像事先計算好了一樣，全部擋了下來！\n\n「沒辦法了……」阿釁咬緊牙關，低聲對前排傳話，「直接用『最後手段』！老巫！把你的考卷，從桌子下面傳給尪伝恺！」\n\n老巫抖著手，趁著高老師「假裝」在看講台上的考卷（其實一直都在看他們）——\n\n「啪。」\n\n「巫同學，」高老師的聲音從前方傳來，「你把考卷塞進書包裡，然後從桌子底下遞給尪同学——這是我第三次提醒你。按照考場規定，桌面以下的一切動作，都視同作弊。」\n\n老巫僵在半空中，考卷還卡在書包裡，整個人像一尊被定身的蠟像。\n\n「老巫！快收回去！」阿釁壓著嗓子喊。\n\n「我、我卡住了！」老巫哭喪著臉，「書包拉鍊勾到考卷了！」\n\n「你！」阿釁氣得差點吐血。\n\n就這麼鬧騰了一整場，收卷鈴聲響起時，全班二十六人的考卷上，全都留著大片大片的空白。\n\n「各位同學，」高老師收完考卷，語氣平和，「明天考數學、後天考自然、大後天考社會。希望大家調整心態，好好作答。」\n\n全班癱在椅子上，眼神一片死灰。\n\n「完蛋了……」老巫喃喃自語，「這次月考，我死定了……」\n\n「還沒結束！」阿釁猛地站起來，眼神裡燃著不甘的火焰，「明天的數學！後天的自然！還有機會！我們還有『人體拼圖』的最後王牌——『互助互答』！」\n\n「可是阿釁，」晴晴平靜地開口，「你覺得，在一個連橡皮擦都不會眨眼睛的老師面前，我們有機會『互助』嗎？」\n\n「……」阿釁沉默了。\n\n接下來的三天，狀況如出一轍。\n\n數學科，阿釁精心策畫的「分段作答」——每個人只寫自己負責的那幾題，其餘留白等待「拼湊」——因為高老師全程無死角監考，根本沒有拼湊的縫隙。全班交出去的考卷，有一半是空白。\n\n自然科，老巫負責的「氣體交換」六題，他背得滾瓜爛熟，但其他題目一題都沒寫。考完試，他哭著對阿釁說：「阿釁，我知道氣體交換，但考卷上問我光合作用啊！」\n\n「那你不會光合作用，為什麼不寫！你背過了啊！」阿釁暴跳如雷。\n\n「因為那不是我的範圍啊！」老巫委屈地大哭，「我的範圍是氣體交換！其他的，是你們的！」\n\n「你！」阿釁氣得頭髮都要炸開了。\n\n社會科，阿釁把全班分成四組，分別負責「台灣地理」「台灣歷史」「台灣文化」「台灣風俗」，打算在考試時「組內互補」。結果，因為高老師的監視，四組之間連一個眼神都傳不過去。\n\n月考結束那天，全班二十六人，像二十六具行屍走肉，飄進教室。\n\n「各位……」阿釁癱在椅子上，聲音虛弱，「我們……徹底失敗了……」\n\n「阿釁，」晴晴突然開口，語氣異常冷靜，「你有沒有發現一件事？」\n\n「什麼事？」\n\n「我們每個人負責的那幾題，」晴晴說，「是不是全都寫對了？」\n\n阿釁一愣：「你怎麼知道？」\n\n「因為我看了。」晴晴推了推眼鏡，「你的『氣體交換』——」\n\n「那是老巫！」\n\n「你的『國語生字』、『數學幾何』，」晴晴補上一刀，「你全都寫對了。」\n\n阿釁張了張嘴，一句話也說不出來。\n\n就在這時，高老師抱著作業簿走進教室。\n\n「各位同學，」他把作業簿放在講台上，「批改成績出來了。在公布之前，我想先給大家看一樣東西。」\n\n他轉身，在黑板上畫出一張密密麻麻的網狀圖：\n\n「這是我在批改考卷時，利用『作業相似度演算法』，比對全班二十六份考卷的結果。」\n\n「這張圖上的每一條線，代表兩個人之間，有一段一模一樣的答案。」\n\n全班倒抽一口涼氣。\n\n「經過比對，」高老師指著黑板，「全班二十六份考卷，共出現了三十七組『完全相同的答案』。」\n\n「而其中，有二十三組——」他頓了頓，「是錯誤的答案。」\n\n「錯誤的？！」阿釁瞪大眼睛。\n\n「對。」高老師平靜地說，「因為，你們『互抄』的部分，抄的其實是彼此『半吊子』的答案。誰記得的那一部分，正確率就高；誰只記得一半的，錯誤率就高。」\n\n他拿起老巫的考卷，指著上面的紅筆標記：\n\n「巫同學，你負責的『氣體交換』六題——全部正確。但你抄來的『光合作用』、『植物分類』——全部錯誤。而且，你的錯誤答案，和班上另外十二個人，錯得一模一樣。」\n\n「十二個人都錯一樣？！」老巫驚呼。\n\n「因為你們抄的是同一個人。」高老師微微一笑，「尪伝恺同學，你記得的『光合作用』是『植物吸二氧化碳、吐氧氣』——」\n\n「對啊！」尪伝恺得意地挺起胸膛。\n\n「——但你漏了『在光照下』這個條件。」高老師補充，「所以，十三個人，一起把『不需要光照』這個錯誤答案，抄上了考卷。」\n\n教室裡響起一片此起彼落的哀嚎聲。\n\n「所以，」高老師放下考卷，語氣誠懇，「這次月考，全班的分數，恰好等於『每個人自己記住的部分』的分數。如果你們把整張考卷，都當成自己『負責』的部分來寫——」\n\n他環視全班，微微一笑：\n\n「——這次月考，全班早就及格了。」\n\n教室裡，鴉雀無聲。\n\n阿釁坐在最後一排，看著黑板上那張紅色的「相似度網狀圖」，看著那些「錯得一模一樣」的記號，第一次，說不出任何豪言壯語。\n\n他低下頭，看著自己那張滿是紅筆標記的考卷——那些自己親手寫的部分，全部是對的；那些等著「拼湊」的空白，全部是錯的。\n\n「……作弊……真的比讀書有用嗎？」阿釁喃喃自語。\n\n窗外的溜溜，趴在通風管口，看著這群垂頭喪氣的皮蛋，尾巴輕輕搖了搖，發出一聲帶點同情、又帶點嘲笑的電子音：\n\n「嗶嗶……人類的『分工合作』……果然，要用在對的地方……」\n\n遠處，周嚴主任正站在辦公室窗前，手裡捏著那本違規登記簿，嘴角緩緩勾起一抹冷笑：\n\n「『作業相似度演算法』是吧……呵，六年一班，你們以為，事情到這裡就結束了嗎？」\n\n他翻開登記簿，在「盯緊」兩個字的下面，又補了一行：\n\n「準備月考補考。","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 5: The Perfect Division of the Twenty-Six\n\nOn the day of the monthly exam, the sky was as gray as a soaked rag.\n\nIn the classroom of Class 6-1, twenty-six desks had been pulled into the standard single-seat exam layout, the surface cleared of books and clutter, leaving only pencil cases, desk pads, and a ruler.\n\nA-Xin sat in the last row. Seizing the moment when Teacher Gao was sorting the exam papers at his desk, he hissed the final orders to Old Wu in the front row:\n\n\"Old Wu! Your part is the 'gas exchange' unit in science! Got it?!\"\n\n\"Got it!\" Old Wu nodded nervously. \"Gas exchange... gas exchange... I'm even exchanging gases in my dreams!\"\n\n\"Also, you're in charge of six questions total, remember, six questions! Leave everything else blank, and wait to copy from us!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin...\" Old Wu asked trembling, \"what if Teacher Gao won't let us copy?\"\n\n\"He'll let us copy!\" A-Xin said firmly. \"Because we have the 'gap tactic'! He's bound to turn his head at some point!\"\n\n\"Everyone,\" Teacher Gao Zhixian's voice came from the podium, \"before the monthly exam officially begins, allow me to remind you—\"\n\nHe paused and pushed up his black-rimmed glasses:\n\n\"According to the Ministry of Education's exam room regulations, proctors must watch the candidates at all times to ensure fairness. So today, I will stand here, from the start of the exam to the end, and I will not turn my head for a single second.\"\n\n\"He won't turn his head for a single second?!\" A-Xin's heart sank with a \"thump.\"\n\n\"Yes.\" Teacher Gao stood still, hands clasped behind his back, like a statue, his gaze sweeping the class like two laser beams. \"Please answer with peace of mind.\"\n\nThe exam began.\n\nA-Xin counted silently in his head: \"In a moment he's bound to blink, wipe his glasses, or look out the window—as long as there's a one-second gap, we strike!\"\n\nHe waited ten full minutes.\n\nTeacher Gao stood nailed to the podium like a surveillance camera, not blinking once.\n\n\"How is that possible...\" sweat beaded on A-Xin's forehead. \"How can a human not blink?!\"\n\nHe decided to manufacture a gap.\n\n\"Clatter!\" A-Xin shoved his pencil case off the desk with a loud crash. \"Oops! Teacher! I dropped my pencil case!\"\n\n\"Mm.\" Teacher Gao's gaze didn't move an inch. \"Please pick it up and continue answering.\"\n\n\"I-I'll also wipe my tears!\" A-Xin crouched down, secretly gesturing to Old Wu to \"get ready to move.\"\n\nTeacher Gao's gaze stuck to A-Xin like glue, utterly motionless.\n\n\"Teacher! There's a bird outside the window!\" Wang Zhuankai suddenly shouted.\n\n\"The bird outside the window,\" Teacher Gao said without turning his head, \"is a gray-faced buzzard, migrating season, flying up from the south. Please continue answering.\"\n\n\"Teacher! The ceiling is dripping!\" Lin Yunyun screamed.\n\n\"That's condensation,\" Teacher Gao replied calmly, \"caused by the high relative humidity in the classroom, water droplets forming at the air conditioner outlet. Please continue answering.\"\n\nA-Xin was utterly in despair.\n\nThis teacher... was simply a wall in human form! No matter how many gaps A-Xin manufactured, Teacher Gao blocked them all as if he'd calculated them in advance!\n\n\"No choice...\" A-Xin gritted his teeth and hissed forward, \"We'll use the 'final measure' directly! Old Wu! Pass your exam paper to Wang Zhuankai under the desk!\"\n\nOld Wu, hands trembling, took advantage of Teacher Gao \"pretending\" to look at the papers on the podium (while actually watching them all along)—\n\n\"Slap.\"\n\n\"Mr. Wu,\" Teacher Gao's voice came from the front, \"you stuffed your exam paper into your backpack, then tried to pass it to Wang under the desk—this is my third reminder. According to exam room regulations, all movement below the desk surface is treated as cheating.\"\n\nOld Wu froze mid-motion, the paper still stuck in his backpack, standing like a wax figure.\n\n\"Old Wu! Put it back quickly!\" A-Xin hissed.\n\n\"I-I'm stuck!\" Old Wu wailed. \"The backpack zipper is caught on the paper!\"\n\n\"You!\" A-Xin was nearly spitting blood.\n\nAnd so the whole exam descended into chaos. When the collection bell rang, the exam papers of all twenty-six students were covered in large stretches of blank space.\n\n\"Everyone,\" Teacher Gao gathered the papers, his tone even, \"tomorrow is math, the day after is science, and the day after that is social studies. I hope everyone adjusts their mindset and answers well.\"\n\nThe whole class collapsed into their chairs, eyes dead.\n\n\"We're doomed...\" Old Wu muttered. \"This monthly exam... I'm finished...\"\n\n\"It's not over yet!\" A-Xin abruptly stood up, the flame of defiance burning in his eyes. \"Tomorrow's math! The day after's science! We still have a chance! We still have the final trump card of the human puzzle—'mutual assistance, mutual answers'!\"\n\n\"But A-Xin,\" Qingqing spoke calmly, \"do you think, in front of a teacher who doesn't even blink his eyes, we have any chance of 'mutual assistance'?\"\n\n\"...\" A-Xin fell silent.\n\nThe next three days went exactly the same way.\n\nFor math, A-Xin's carefully planned \"segmented answering\"—everyone writing only the questions they were assigned and leaving the rest blank to be \"pieced together\"—fell apart because Teacher Gao's all-round supervision left no gaps to piece anything together. Half of the papers the class submitted were blank.\n\nFor science, Old Wu had memorized his six \"gas exchange\" questions inside and out, but he didn't write a single other question. After the exam, he wept to A-Xin: \"A-Xin, I know gas exchange, but the paper asked about photosynthesis!\"\n\n\"Then if you don't know photosynthesis, why didn't you write it? You've studied it before!\" A-Xin stamped his foot in fury.\n\n\"Because it's not my section!\" Old Wu burst into tears. \"My section is gas exchange! Everything else is yours!\"\n\n\"You!\" A-Xin's hair was practically standing on end.\n\nFor social studies, A-Xin divided the class into four groups, respectively in charge of \"Taiwan's geography,\" \"Taiwan's history,\" \"Taiwan's culture,\" and \"Taiwan's customs,\" planning \"intra-group mutual supplementation\" during the exam. As a result, because of Teacher Gao's surveillance, not even a single meaningful glance could pass between the groups.\n\nThe day the monthly exam ended, all twenty-six students drifted into the classroom like twenty-six zombies.\n\n\"Everyone...\" A-Xin slumped into his chair, his voice weak. \"We... have completely failed...\"\n\n\"A-Xin,\" Qingqing suddenly spoke, her tone unusually calm, \"have you noticed something?\"\n\n\"What?\"\n\n\"The questions each of us was responsible for,\" Qingqing said, \"didn't we all get them right?\"\n\nA-Xin was taken aback: \"How do you know?\"\n\n\"Because I looked.\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses. \"Your 'gas exchange'—\"\n\n\"That was Old Wu's!\"\n\n\"Your 'Chinese new words,' your 'math geometry,'\" Qingqing delivered the finishing blow, \"you got all of them right.\"\n\nA-Xin opened his mouth but couldn't say a word.\n\nJust then, Teacher Gao walked in carrying a stack of notebooks.\n\n\"Everyone,\" he set the notebooks on the podium, \"the grading results are out. Before I announce them, I'd like to show you something first.\"\n\nHe turned and drew a dense web of lines on the blackboard:\n\n\"This is the result of comparing all twenty-six of your exam papers using the 'homework similarity algorithm.'\"\n\n\"Every line in this diagram represents two people who had an identical segment of answers.\"\n\nThe whole class gasped.\n\n\"After comparison,\" Teacher Gao pointed at the blackboard, \"across all twenty-six exam papers, thirty-seven pairs of 'completely identical answers' were found.\"\n\n\"And of those—\" he paused, \"twenty-three pairs are wrong answers.\"\n\n\"Wrong?!\" A-Xin widened his eyes.\n\n\"Yes.\" Teacher Gao said calmly. \"Because the parts you 'copied from each other' were copying each other's 'half-baked' answers. Whoever remembered their section well had high accuracy; whoever only remembered half had high error rates.\"\n\nHe picked up Old Wu's paper and pointed at the red marks:\n\n\"Mr. Wu, your six 'gas exchange' questions—all correct. But the 'photosynthesis' and 'plant classification' you copied—all wrong. Moreover, your wrong answers are wrong in exactly the same way as twelve other students in the class.\"\n\n\"Twelve people wrong the same way?!\" Old Wu exclaimed.\n\n\"Because you copied from the same person.\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly. \"Wang Zhuankai remembered 'photosynthesis' as 'plants take in carbon dioxide and release oxygen'—\"\n\n\"Right!\" Wang Zhuankai puffed out his chest smugly.\n\n\"—but you missed the condition 'under light.'\" Teacher Gao added. \"So thirteen people copied the wrong answer 'no light needed' onto their papers together.\"\n\nA chorus of agonized wails rippled through the classroom.\n\n\"So,\" Teacher Gao put down the paper, his tone sincere, \"in this monthly exam, the whole class's scores are exactly equal to the scores of 'the parts each person remembered themselves.' If you had treated the entire exam as the 'section you were responsible for' and written it—\"\n\nHe swept his gaze across the class and smiled faintly:\n\n\"—this monthly exam, the whole class would already have passed.\"\n\nThe classroom was utterly silent.\n\nA-Xin sat in the last row, looking at the red \"similarity web\" on the blackboard, looking at all those marks of \"wrong in exactly the same way,\" and for the first time, he couldn't produce any grand declaration.\n\nHe lowered his head and looked at his own paper covered in red marks—the parts he'd written himself were all correct; the blanks waiting to be \"pieced together\" were all wrong.\n\n\"...Is cheating really more useful than studying?\" A-Xin muttered to himself.\n\nOutside the window, Liu-Liu lay at the ventilation duct, watching this group of crestfallen trouble-makers, its tail swaying gently, letting out an electronic sound that was part sympathy, part mockery:\n\n\"Beep beep... human 'division of labor'... really should be used in the right place...\"\n\nFar away, Director Zhou Yan stood by the office window, clutching the infraction notebook, a cold smile slowly curling at the corner of his mouth:\n\n\"The 'homework similarity algorithm,' huh... hmph, Class 6-1, you don't think this is over, do you?\"\n\nHe flipped open his notebook and, beneath the words \"Keep a close watch,\" added another line:\n\n\"Prepare for the monthly exam make-up test.\""},{"id":6,"rawContent":"# 《全班作弊中》\n\n## 第六章：月考大戰之全軍覆沒\n\n月考放榜那天，鹿陽國小的中庭公布欄前，擠得水洩不通。\n\n阿釁、老巫、晴晴三人擠在最前面，二十六雙眼睛死死盯著那張鮮紅的成績單。\n\n「怎麼辦怎麼辦怎麼辦……」老巫緊張得連手上的肉包都忘了咬，整個人在原地轉圈圈，「阿釁，我、我不敢看……」\n\n「怕什麼！大不了就是……就是……」阿釁的聲音也開始抖，「就是真的死定了……」\n\n「找到了！」眼尖的晴晴伸出手，指著六年一班那一欄，「你們看！」\n\n三顆頭「唰」地湊了過去。\n\n下一秒——\n\n「啊啊啊啊啊啊——！」\n\n老巫發出一聲驚天動地的慘叫，整個人向後一倒，一屁股摔坐在地上，淚水奪眶而出：\n\n「我及格了！我及格了！我自然考了七十八分！阿釁！我考了七十八分！」\n\n「七十八分？！」阿釁衝上前，一把搶過成績單，瞪大眼睛，「你上次不是才四十五分嗎？！」\n\n「我、我也不知道啊！」老巫又哭又笑，「我只是把那個什麼『氣體交換』背得很熟，然後考卷上的題目，好像突然都會了！」\n\n「我也及格了！」尪伝恺從人群中擠出來，興奮地揮著成績單，「我國語七十一分！上上次我才五十五分！」\n\n「你怎麼考的？」阿釁問。\n\n「我也不知道！」尪伝恺抓著頭，「我就是……為了把生字註解『縮小』寫進橡皮擦裡，把那幾課的國語，反反覆覆看了十幾遍……」\n\n「縮小小抄，結果把課文背起來了？」阿釁喃喃自語。\n\n「對啊！」尪伝恺笑得合不攏嘴，「現在那些生字，我閉著眼睛都會寫了！」\n\n人群中，歡呼聲此起彼落。\n\n二十六個人裡，有二十個人刷新了自己六年級以來的最高分；全班平均，比上一次月考，整整進步了十三分。\n\n「進步十三分！」阿釁看著成績單，難以置信，「我們明明……作弊全軍覆沒了啊！」\n\n「我們作戰全軍覆沒，」晴晴推了推眼鏡，語氣平靜，「但我們『為了作戰而準備』的內容，全部都記住了。」\n\n阿釁愣住了。\n\n他低頭看看成績單，又抬頭看看那群興奮得手舞足蹈的同學——老巫在跳、尪伝恺在叫、林芸芸捧著自己的成績單哭得稀哩嘩啦。\n\n「林芸芸！妳怎麼哭了？」阿釁衝過去。\n\n「我……我第一次考及格……」林芸芸哽咽著，「我、我是為了把小抄寫進鉛筆盒夾層，把那張重點背了二十遍……」\n\n「背了二十遍……」阿釁喃喃自語，眼神慢慢變得複雜。\n\n就在這時，一道陰影籠罩下來。\n\n「哼！」\n\n周嚴主任倒背著雙手，站在人群外圍，鷹隼般的目光掃過那張成績單，臉色陰晴不定：\n\n「六年一班……平均進步十三分？！」\n\n他湊近成績單，看了又看，越看越不甘心：「這不可能！你們這群皮蛋，月考那幾天明明在搞『人體拼圖』！怎麼可能考出這種成績？！」\n\n「報告主任，」高老師不知何時出現在他身後，語氣平淡，「六年一班的學生，雖然作弊方式笨拙，但他們在準備作弊的過程中，確實把課本內容都背下來了。這叫『有效的學習動機』。」\n\n「有效……什麼？」周嚴瞪大眼睛。\n\n「簡而言之，」高老師微微一笑，「他們以為自己在作弊，其實是在讀書。」\n\n「——！」周嚴張了張嘴，最後只能悻悻地哼一聲，「哼！月考僥倖，期末考就沒這麼好運了！我盯緊你們！」\n\n他甩袖離去，留下全場一陣勝利的歡呼。\n\n放學時分，校門口的接送區，成了第二個「戰場」。\n\n柯媽媽一手拎著手機，一手叉腰，堵在六年一班的隊伍前面，銳利的目光掃過人群：\n\n「我看看……我看看……進步十三分是吧？」\n\n「是的，柯媽媽。」高老師點頭。\n\n「哼，」柯媽媽揚起下巴，「才進步十三分，就想跟人家說嘴？期末考，我們班要全班一半以上擠進校排前一百名！辦不到，我就把成績單寄到教育局！」\n\n「柯媽媽，成績不能這樣……」\n\n「我不管！期末考，我只看分數！」\n\n另一頭，老巫爸爸的機車停在樹蔭下，看到老巫滿面笑容地跑來，得意地晃了晃手中的雞腿：\n\n「小巫啊！爸爸聽說了！你自然考了七十八分？及格啦？」\n\n「對！爸！我及格了！」老巫興奮地點頭。\n\n「好！有出息！今晚加菜！一整隻烤雞！」老巫爸爸大笑，然後話鋒一轉，「——不過呢，期末考要是能考八十分，爸爸就請你吃一個月雞腿！」\n\n「一個月雞腿！」老巫的眼睛瞬間亮得像兩顆小太陽，「為了雞腿，我拼了！」\n\n最後，是阿釁。\n\n他站在校門口，手裡捏著手機，螢幕上是媽媽傳來的訊息：\n\n「阿釁：月考過了，遊戲機密碼我放你鉛筆盒了。期末考要是退了，密碼收回。」\n\n阿釁握著手機，臉上卻沒有想像中的狂喜。\n\n他慢慢地、慢慢地，把手機放進口袋，抬頭看向夕陽下那片橘紅色的天空，腦海裡不斷迴盪著高老師剛才那句話：\n\n「他們以為自己在作弊，其實是在讀書。」\n\n「……作弊……讀書……」阿釁喃喃自語，「這兩個東西……怎麼好像……越來越分不清了？」\n\n「阿釁！」\n\n晴晴從後面追上來，手上還拎著一個小袋子：「你站在這裡發什麼呆？明天要開始準備期末考了！」\n\n「期末考？！」阿釁嚇了一跳，「不是還有一個多月嗎？」\n\n「你媽的訊息我看到了。」晴晴晃了晃手機，「期末考要是退了，遊戲機密碼收回。柯媽媽也放話了，全班一半以上進校排前一百。你覺得，我們還有時間悠哉嗎？」\n\n阿釁沉默了。\n\n他低頭想了很久很久，然後，猛地抬頭，眼中重新燃起熊熊鬥志：\n\n「好！既然月考的『人體拼圖』失敗了，那我們就——科技革命！」\n\n「科技？」晴晴挑眉。\n\n「對！第四號計畫！」阿釁握緊拳頭，「月考靠『背』，我們就作弊輸在『被看到』！期末考，我們要用一種『高老師看不見』的方法！」\n\n「高老師連紙飛機、暗號都看得見，」晴晴平靜地補刀，「你覺得，有什麼是『看不見』的？」\n\n「那就……」阿釁神秘一笑，「做一種『看不見的』作弊工具！」\n\n隔天，課堂上。\n\n高老師站在講台上，正準備講解月考的錯誤考題，突然，他的眼鏡鏡片「啪」地閃了一下，緊接著，一道刺眼的強光從他瞳孔中暴射而出——\n\n「嗤啦——！」\n\n黑板上，赫然投影出整份考卷的「標準答案」！\n\n「是答案！」老巫「唰」地站起來，手忙腳亂地抽出筆，「快抄！快抄！」\n\n「抄什麼抄！」阿釁撲過去一把壓住老巫的手，「上次我們都看過了，這次根本不用抄！」\n\n「咦？」老巫愣住，低頭看了看自己的考卷，「對……對耶……這題我剛才就寫對了……」\n\n「全班都寫對了。」晴晴推了推眼鏡，「因為這些題目，我們昨天才複習過。」\n\n投影持續了三秒鐘，才被高老師自己「啪」地關掉。\n\n「抱歉，」高老師面色平靜地推了推眼鏡，「光學投影系統出現暫時性故障。各位同學，請繼續檢討考卷。」\n\n教室裡，二十六雙眼睛，齊刷刷地盯著黑板上那抹殘留的光影。\n\n沒有任何人低頭抄寫。\n\n「老師，」阿釁舉起手，語氣帶著一點說不出的得意，「這次不用投影了。這些題目，我們全班都會了。」\n\n「很好。」高老師微微一笑，「那就請全班，把這份考卷，重新做一遍——這次，看看誰真的『會了』。」\n\n全班二十六人，齊刷刷地低頭，開始作答。\n\n陽光透過窗戶，灑在每一張專注的小臉上。\n\n窗外的溜溜，趴在通風管口，尾巴輕輕搖晃，電子眼裡閃爍著複雜的光芒：\n\n「嗶嗶……偵測到『誠實指數』……正在以緩慢而穩定的速度……上升中……」\n\n而走廊盡頭的辦公室裡，周嚴主任正對著那本違規登記簿，皺著眉頭，一筆一劃地寫下：\n\n「期末考，重點盯防：六年一班。」\n\n「我倒要看看，這群皮蛋，能把『作弊』玩出什麼花樣。」","rawContentEn":"# *The Whole Class Is Cheating*\n\n## Chapter 6: The Month Exam Battle: Total Defeat\n\nThe day the monthly exam results were posted, the central courtyard of Luyang Elementary was packed solid.\n\nA-Xin, Old Wu, and Qingqing squeezed to the front, twenty-six pairs of eyes fixed on the bright red results board.\n\n\"What do we do, what do we do, what do we do...\" Old Wu was so nervous he forgot to bite his pork bun, spinning in circles on the spot. \"A-Xin, I, I don't dare look...\"\n\n\"What's there to be afraid of! At worst... at worst...\" A-Xin's voice began to shake too. \"At worst, we're really, truly done for...\"\n\n\"Found it!\" Sharp-eyed Qingqing reached out, pointing at the Class 6-1 column. \"Look!\"\n\nThree heads \"snapped\" over at once.\n\nThe next second—\n\n\"Ahhhhhhh—!\"\n\nOld Wu let out an earth-shaking scream, stumbling backward and landing flat on the ground, tears streaming: \"I passed! I passed! I scored seventy-eight in science! A-Xin! I scored seventy-eight!\"\n\n\"Seventy-eight?!\" A-Xin rushed over, snatching the results sheet, eyes wide. \"Weren't you at forty-five last time?!\"\n\n\"I-I don't know either!\" Old Wu laughed and cried at once. \"I just memorized that 'gas exchange' really well, and then all the questions on the paper suddenly seemed like I knew them!\"\n\n\"I passed too!\" Wang Zhuankai squeezed out of the crowd, waving his results sheet excitedly. \"I scored seventy-one in Chinese! Last time, I only got fifty-five!\"\n\n\"How did you do it?\" A-Xin asked.\n\n\"I don't know either!\" Wang Zhuankai scratched his head. \"I just... to shrink the new-word annotations into the eraser, I read those Chinese lessons over and over, maybe a dozen times...\"\n\n\"Shrinking a cheat sheet, and ended up memorizing the text?\" A-Xin muttered.\n\n\"Right!\" Wang Zhuankai grinned from ear to ear. \"Now I can write those new words with my eyes closed!\"\n\nCheers rippled through the crowd.\n\nOut of the twenty-six, twenty had set new personal bests since sixth grade; the class average had improved a full thirteen points over the last monthly exam.\n\n\"Up thirteen points!\" A-Xin stared at the results sheet in disbelief. \"We... we were caught at every single cheat plan!\"\n\n\"Our battles were all wiped out,\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses, her tone calm, \"but the content we 'prepared for the battles'—we remembered all of it.\"\n\nA-Xin froze.\n\nHe looked down at the results sheet, then up at the group of classmates jumping and cheering—Old Wu hopping, Wang Zhuankai shouting, Lin Yunyun clutching her own results sheet and crying her heart out.\n\n\"Lin Yunyun! Why are you crying?\" A-Xin rushed over.\n\n\"I... I passed for the first time...\" Lin Yunyun sobbed. \"I, I memorized that key-point sheet twenty times so I could hide it in my pencil case...\"\n\n\"Twenty times...\" A-Xin muttered, his gaze slowly turning complicated.\n\nJust then, a shadow descended.\n\n\"Hmph!\"\n\nDirector Zhou Yan stood with his hands clasped behind his back at the edge of the crowd, his hawk-sharp gaze sweeping over the results sheet, his face darkening with reluctance:\n\n\"Class 6-1... a thirteen-point class average improvement?!\"\n\nHe leaned in, looked at the sheet again and again, and grew more and more unwilling to accept it: \"Impossible! You little trouble-makers were busy doing your 'human puzzle' during the exam days! How could you score like this?!\"\n\n\"Director,\" Teacher Gao appeared behind him without a sound, his tone flat, \"although the students of Class 6-1 used clumsy cheating methods, in the process of preparing to cheat, they did indeed memorize the textbook content. This is called 'effective learning motivation.'\"\n\n\"Effective... what?\" Director Zhou stared wide-eyed.\n\n\"To put it simply,\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly, \"they thought they were cheating, but they were actually studying.\"\n\n\"—!\" Director Zhou opened his mouth, then could only grumble, \"Hmph! You got lucky on the monthly exam! You won't be so lucky on the final exam! I'll keep a close watch on you!\"\n\nHe swept away, leaving the class to their victorious cheers.\n\nAt dismissal, the pickup zone at the school gate became the second \"battlefield.\"\n\nMama Ke, one hand holding her phone, the other on her hip, blocked the front of the Class 6-1 lineup, her sharp gaze sweeping through the crowd:\n\n\"Let me see... let me see... up thirteen points, right?\"\n\n\"Yes, Mama Ke.\" Teacher Gao nodded.\n\n\"Hmph,\" Mama Ke lifted her chin, \"a mere thirteen points and you're already talking big? On the final exam, I want more than half the class in the school's top one hundred! Otherwise, I'll mail the results straight to the Bureau of Education!\"\n\n\"Mama Ke, grades can't be treated this way...\"\n\n\"I don't care! On the final exam, I only look at scores!\"\n\nOver on the other side, Old Wu's father's scooter was parked in the shade. Seeing Old Wu come running with a beaming face, he proudly waved his drumstick:\n\n\"Little Wu! Dad heard! You got seventy-eight in science? You passed?\"\n\n\"Yeah! Dad! I passed!\" Old Wu nodded excitedly.\n\n\"Good! That's my boy! Extra dishes tonight! A whole roasted chicken!\" Old Wu's father laughed, then shifted gears. \"—However, if you can score eighty on the final exam, I'll treat you to a month of drumsticks!\"\n\n\"A month of drumsticks!\" Old Wu's eyes instantly blazed like two little suns. \"For the drumsticks, I'll give it my all!\"\n\nLast was A-Xin.\n\nHe stood at the school gate, phone in hand, the screen showing his mother's message:\n\n\"A-Xin: You passed the monthly exam, so I put the game console password in your pencil case. If you slip on the final exam, the password comes back to me.\"\n\nA-Xin gripped the phone, but his face held none of the expected joy.\n\nSlowly, slowly, he put the phone in his pocket, raised his head to look at the orange-red sky under the setting sun, Teacher Gao's words from just now echoing endlessly through his mind:\n\n\"They thought they were cheating, but they were actually studying.\"\n\n\"...Cheating... studying...\" A-Xin muttered. \"These two things... how come they seem... more and more impossible to tell apart?\"\n\n\"A-Xin!\"\n\nQingqing caught up from behind, a small bag dangling from her hand: \"What are you standing here spacing out for? We need to start preparing for the final exam tomorrow!\"\n\n\"The final exam?!\" A-Xin jumped in fright. \"Isn't that over a month away?\"\n\n\"I saw your mom's message.\" Qingqing waved her phone. \"If you slip on the final exam, the game console password comes back. Mama Ke also made her demand—more than half the class in the school's top one hundred. Do you think we have time to take it easy?\"\n\nA-Xin fell silent.\n\nHe bowed his head and thought for a long, long time.\n\nThen, he abruptly looked up, fresh fighting spirit blazing in his eyes:\n\n\"Fine! Since the monthly exam's 'human puzzle' failed, we'll have—the technology revolution!\"\n\n\"Technology?\" Qingqing raised an eyebrow.\n\n\"Yes! Plan No. 4!\" A-Xin clenched his fist. \"In the monthly exam we relied on 'memorizing,' and we lost because we were 'seen'! For the final exam, we'll use a method that Teacher Gao 'can't see'!\"\n\n\"Teacher Gao can even see paper planes and codes,\" Qingqing delivered the finishing blow calmly, \"do you think there's anything he 'can't see'?\"\n\n\"Then—\" A-Xin smiled mysteriously, \"we'll make a cheating tool that's 'invisible'!\"\n\nThe next day, in class.\n\nTeacher Gao stood on the podium, just about to explain the wrong answers from the monthly exam, when suddenly his glasses \"flashed,\" and a moment later, a blinding light burst from his pupils—\n\n\"Sssss-crackle!\"\n\nOn the blackboard, the \"standard answers\" to the entire exam paper appeared in projection!\n\n\"It's the answers!\" Old Wu \"shot\" to his feet, fumbling for his pen. \"Quick, copy them! Copy them fast!\"\n\n\"Copy what!?\" A-Xin lunged over and pressed down on Old Wu's hand. \"We all know these now! There's nothing to copy!\"\n\n\"Huh?\" Old Wu froze, lowering his head to look at his own paper. \"Right... right... I already wrote this one correctly just now...\"\n\n\"The whole class wrote them correctly.\" Qingqing pushed up her glasses. \"Because we reviewed these questions yesterday.\"\n\nThe projection lasted three seconds before Teacher Gao shut it off himself with a \"click.\"\n\n\"My apologies,\" Teacher Gao pushed up his glasses, his face calm, \"the optical projection system has a temporary malfunction. Everyone, please continue reviewing the exam.\"\n\nIn the classroom, twenty-six pairs of eyes stared at the lingering light on the blackboard.\n\nNobody lowered their head to copy anything.\n\n\"Teacher,\" A-Xin raised his hand, his tone carrying a hint of indefinable pride, \"no need for the projection this time. The whole class already knows these questions.\"\n\n\"Very good.\" Teacher Gao smiled faintly. \"Then let the whole class do this exam paper again—this time, let's see who really 'knows it.'\"\n\nAll twenty-six students lowered their heads in unison and began writing.\n\nSunlight streamed through the window, spilling across every focused little face.\n\nOutside the window, Liu-Liu lay at the ventilation duct, its tail swaying gently, a complex light flickering in its electronic eyes:\n\n\"Beep beep... detecting the 'honesty index'... rising slowly but steadily...\"\n\nAnd in the office at the end of the hallway, Director Zhou Yan frowned at the infraction notebook, writing stroke by stroke:\n\n\"Final exam, key surveillance target: Class 6-1.\"\n\n\"Let's see what tricks these trouble-makers can pull with their 'cheating.'\""}];
